\c 1
\s1 The Beginning of Knowledge
\r (\ref Proverbs 9:1–12|PRO 9:1-12\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb These are the proverbs|מִ֭שְׁלֵי\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb king|מֶ֝֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 2 \rb for gaining|לָדַ֣עַת\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֣ה\rb* \rb and discipline|וּמוּסָ֑ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb for comprehending|לְ֝הָבִ֗ין\rb* \rb words|אִמְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of insight|בִינָֽה׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 3 \rb and for receiving|לָ֭קַחַת\rb* \rb instruction|מוּסַ֣ר\rb* \rb in wise living|הַשְׂכֵּ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and in righteousness|צֶ֥דֶק\rb*, \rb justice|וּ֝מִשְׁפָּ֗ט\rb*, \rb and equity|וּמֵישָׁרִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb To impart|לָתֵ֣ת\rb* \rb prudence|עָרְמָ֑ה\rb* \rb to the simple|לִפְתָאיִ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 1:4 \ft The Hebrew word rendered \fqa simple \ft in Proverbs refers to one who is naive, without moral direction, or inclined to evil.\f*
\q2 \rb and knowledge|דַּ֣עַת\rb* \rb and discretion|וּמְזִמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb to the young|לְ֝נַ֗עַר\rb*,
\q1 \v 5 \rb let the wise|חָ֭כָם\rb* \rb listen|יִשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb and gain|וְי֣וֹסֶף\rb* \rb instruction|לֶ֑קַח\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the discerning|וְ֝נָב֗וֹן\rb* \rb acquire|יִקְנֶֽה׃\rb* \rb wise counsel|תַּחְבֻּל֥וֹת\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb by understanding|לְהָבִ֣ין\rb* \rb the proverbs|מָ֭שָׁל\rb* \rb and parables|וּמְלִיצָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb the sayings|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb and riddles|וְחִידֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb of the wise|חֲ֝כָמִ֗ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb The fear|יִרְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb is the beginning|רֵאשִׁ֣ית\rb* \rb of knowledge|דָּ֑עַת\rb*,
\q2 \rb but fools|אֱוִילִ֥ים\rb*\f + \fr 1:7 \ft The Hebrew words rendered as \fqa fool \ft in Proverbs denote one who is morally deficient.\f* \rb despise|בָּֽזוּ׃פ\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֥ה\rb* \rb and discipline|וּ֝מוּסָ֗ר\rb*.
\s1 The Enticement of Sin
\q1 \v 8 \rb Listen|שְׁמַ֣ע\rb*, \rb my son|בְּ֭נִי\rb*, \rb to your father’s|אָבִ֑יךָ\rb* \rb instruction|מוּסַ֣ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and do not forsake|תִּ֝טֹּ֗שׁ\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb the teaching|תּוֹרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of your mother|אִמֶּֽךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb For|כִּ֤י׀\rb* \rb they|הֵ֬ם\rb* \rb are a garland|לִוְיַ֤ת\rb* \rb of grace|חֵ֓ן\rb* \rb on your head|לְרֹאשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and a pendant|וַ֝עֲנָקִ֗ים\rb* \rb around your neck|לְגַרְגְּרֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb My son|בְּנִ֡י\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb sinners|חַ֝טָּאִ֗ים\rb* \rb entice you|יְפַתּ֥וּךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb yield to them|תֹּבֵֽא׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb they say|יֹאמְרוּ֮\rb*, “\rb Come|לְכָ֪ה\rb* \rb along|אִ֫תָּ֥נוּ\rb*, \rb let us lie in wait|נֶאֶרְבָ֥ה\rb* \rb for blood|לְדָ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb let us ambush|נִצְפְּנָ֖ה\rb* \rb the innocent|לְנָקִ֣י\rb* \rb without cause|חִנָּֽם׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 12 \rb let us swallow them|נִ֭בְלָעֵם\rb* \rb alive|חַיִּ֑ים\rb* \rb like Sheol|כִּשְׁא֣וֹל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and whole|וּ֝תְמִימִ֗ים\rb* \rb like those descending|כְּי֣וֹרְדֵי\rb* \rb into the Pit|בֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb We will find|נִמְצָ֑א\rb* \rb all manner|כָּל־\rb* \rb of precious|יָקָ֣ר\rb* \rb goods|ה֣וֹן\rb*;
\q2 \rb we will fill|נְמַלֵּ֖א\rb* \rb our houses|בָתֵּ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb with plunder|שָׁלָֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb Throw in|תַּפִּ֣יל\rb* \rb your lot|גּ֭וֹרָ֣לְךָ\rb* \rb with us|בְּתוֹכֵ֑נוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb let us all|לְכֻלָּֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb share|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb one|אֶ֝חָ֗ד\rb* \rb purse|כִּ֥יס\rb*” —
\q1 \v 15 \rb my son|בְּנִ֗י\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb walk|תֵּלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb the road|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb with them|אִתָּ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb or set|מְנַ֥ע\rb* \rb foot|רַ֝גְלְךָ֗\rb* \rb upon their path|מִנְּתִיבָתָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb their feet|רַ֭גְלֵיהֶם\rb* \rb run|יָר֑וּצוּ\rb* \rb to evil|לָרַ֣ע\rb*,
\q2 \rb and they are swift|וִֽ֝ימַהֲר֗וּ\rb* \rb to shed|לִשְׁפָּךְ־\rb* \rb blood|דָּֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb How|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb futile it is|חִ֭נָּם\rb* \rb to spread|מְזֹרָ֣ה\rb* \rb the net|הָרָ֑שֶׁת\rb*
\q2 \rb where any|כָל־\rb* \rb bird|בַּ֥עַל\rb*\rb |כָּנָֽף׃\rb* \rb can see it|בְּ֝עֵינֵ֗י\rb*!
\q1 \v 18 \rb But they|וְ֭הֵם\rb* \rb lie in wait|יֶאֱרֹ֑בוּ\rb* \rb for their own blood|לְדָמָ֣ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb they ambush|יִ֝צְפְּנ֗וּ\rb* \rb their own lives|לְנַפְשֹׁתָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb Such is|כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb the fate|אָ֭רְחוֹת\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who are greedy|בֹּ֣צֵֽעַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb whose unjust gain|בָּ֑צַע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb takes|יִקָּֽח׃פ\rb* \rb the lives|נֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of its possessors|בְּעָלָ֣יו\rb*.
\s1 Wisdom Calls Aloud
\q1 \v 20 \rb Wisdom|חָ֭כְמוֹת\rb* \rb calls out|תָּרֹ֑נָּה\rb* \rb in the street|בַּח֣וּץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb she lifts|תִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb her voice|קוֹלָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb in the square|בָּ֝רְחֹב֗וֹת\rb*;
\q1 \v 21 \rb in the main|בְּרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb concourse|הֹמִיּ֗וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 1:21 \ft Or \fqa from the top of the wall\f* \rb she cries aloud|תִּ֫קְרָ֥א\rb*,
\q2 \rb at the city|בָּעִ֗יר\rb*\rb |בְּפִתְחֵ֖י\rb* \rb gates|שְׁעָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb she makes|תֹאמֵֽר׃\rb* \rb her speech|אֲמָרֶ֥יהָ\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 22 “\rb How|עַד־\rb* \rb long|מָתַ֣י׀\rb*, \rb O simple ones|פְּתָיִם֮\rb*, \rb will you love|תְּֽאֵהֲב֫וּ\rb* \rb your simple ways|פֶ֥תִי\rb*?
\q2 \rb How long will scoffers|וְלֵצִ֗ים\rb* \rb delight|חָמְד֣וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb in their scorn|לָ֭צוֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb and fools|וּ֝כְסִילִ֗ים\rb* \rb hate|יִשְׂנְאוּ־\rb* \rb knowledge|דָֽעַת׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 23 \rb If you had repented|תָּשׁ֗וּבוּ\rb* \rb at my rebuke|לְֽת֫וֹכַחְתִּ֥י\rb*,
\q2 \rb then surely|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb I would have poured out|אַבִּ֣יעָה\rb* \rb my|לָכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb spirit on you|רוּחִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I would have made|אוֹדִ֖יעָה\rb* \rb my words|דְבָרַ֣י\rb* \rb known to you|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb Because|יַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you refused|וַתְּמָאֵ֑נוּ\rb* \rb my call|קָ֭רָאתִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb and no one|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb took|מַקְשִֽׁיב׃\rb* \rb my outstretched|נָטִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb hand|יָ֝דִ֗י\rb*,
\q1 \v 25 \rb because you neglected|וַתִּפְרְע֥וּ\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb my counsel|עֲצָתִ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and wanted|אֲבִיתֶֽם׃\rb* \rb none|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb of my correction|וְ֝תוֹכַחְתִּ֗י\rb*,
\q1 \v 26 \rb in turn|גַּם־\rb* \rb I|אֲ֭נִי\rb* \rb will mock|אֶשְׂחָ֑ק\rb* \rb your calamity|בְּאֵידְכֶ֣ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will sneer|אֶ֝לְעַ֗ג\rb* \rb when terror|פַחְדְּכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb strikes you|בְּבֹ֣א\rb*,
\q1 \v 27 \rb when your dread|פַּחְדְּכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb comes|בְּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb like a storm|כְשַׁאֲוָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and your destruction|וְֽ֭אֵידְכֶם\rb*\rb |יֶאֱתֶ֑ה\rb* \rb like a whirlwind|כְּסוּפָ֣ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb when distress|צָרָ֥ה\rb* \rb and anguish|וְצוּקָֽה׃\rb* \rb overwhelm you|בְּבֹ֥א\rb*\rb |עֲ֝לֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 28 \rb Then|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb they will call on me|יִ֭קְרָאֻנְנִי\rb*, \rb but I will not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb answer|אֶֽעֱנֶ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb they will earnestly seek me|יְ֝שַׁחֲרֻ֗נְנִי\rb*, \rb but will not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb find me|יִמְצָאֻֽנְנִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 29 \rb |תַּ֭חַת\rb* \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb they hated|שָׂ֣נְאוּ\rb* \rb knowledge|דָ֑עַת\rb*
\q2 \rb and chose|בָחָֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to fear|וְיִרְאַ֥ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֝הֹוָ֗ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 30 \rb They accepted|אָב֥וּ\rb* \rb none|לֹא־\rb* \rb of my counsel|לַעֲצָתִ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb they despised|נָ֝אֲצ֗וּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my reproof|תּוֹכַחְתִּֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 31 \rb So they will eat|וְֽ֭יֹאכְלוּ\rb* \rb the fruit|מִפְּרִ֣י\rb* \rb of their own way|דַרְכָּ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and be filled|יִשְׂבָּֽעוּ׃\rb* \rb with their own devices|וּֽמִמֹּעֲצֹ֖תֵיהֶ֣ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 32 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the waywardness|מְשׁוּבַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the simple|פְּתָיִ֣ם\rb* \rb will slay them|תַּֽהַרְגֵ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the complacency|וְשַׁלְוַ֖ת\rb* \rb of fools|כְּסִילִ֣ים\rb* \rb will destroy them|תְּאַבְּדֵֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 33 \rb But whoever listens|וְשֹׁמֵ֣עַֽ\rb* \rb to me|לִ֭י\rb* \rb will dwell|יִשְׁכָּן־\rb* \rb in safety|בֶּ֑טַח\rb*,
\q2 \rb secure|וְ֝שַׁאֲנַ֗ן\rb* \rb from the fear|מִפַּ֥חַד\rb* \rb of evil|רָעָֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 2
\s1 The Benefits of Wisdom
\q1 \v 1 \rb My son|בְּ֭נִי\rb*, \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you accept|תִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb my words|אֲמָרָ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and hide|תִּצְפֹּ֥ן\rb* \rb my commandments|וּ֝מִצְוֺתַ֗י\rb* \rb within you|אִתָּֽךְ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 2 \rb if you incline|לְהַקְשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb your ear|אָזְנֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb to wisdom|לַֽחָכְמָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and direct|תַּטֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb your heart|לִ֝בְּךָ֗\rb* \rb to understanding|לַתְּבוּנָֽה׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 3 \rb if you|אִ֣ם\rb* \rb truly|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb call out|תִקְרָ֑א\rb* \rb to insight|לַבִּינָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and lift|תִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb your voice|קוֹלֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb to understanding|לַ֝תְּבוּנָ֗ה\rb*,
\q1 \v 4 \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you seek|תְּבַקְשֶׁ֥נָּה\rb* \rb it like silver|כַכָּ֑סֶף\rb*
\q2 \rb and search it out|תַּחְפְּשֶֽׂנָּה׃\rb* \rb like hidden treasure|וְֽכַמַּטְמוֹנִ֥ים\rb*,
\q1 \v 5 \rb then|אָ֗ז\rb* \rb you will discern|תָּ֭בִין\rb* \rb the fear|יִרְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and discover|תִּמְצָֽא׃\rb* \rb the knowledge|וְדַ֖עַת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb gives|יִתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb from His mouth|מִ֝פִּ֗יו\rb* \rb come knowledge|דַּ֣עַת\rb* \rb and understanding|וּתְבוּנָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb He stores up|וְצָפַן\rb* \rb sound wisdom|תּוּשִׁיָּ֑ה\rb* \rb for the upright|לַ֭יְשָׁרִים\rb*;
\q2 \rb He is a shield|מָ֝גֵ֗ן\rb* \rb to those who walk|לְהֹ֣לְכֵי\rb* \rb with integrity|תֹֽם׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 8 \rb to guard|לִ֭נְצֹר\rb* \rb the paths|אָרְח֣וֹת\rb* \rb of justice|מִשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb*
\q2 \rb and protect|יִשְׁמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb the way|וְדֶ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb of His saints|חֲסִידוֹ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb Then|אָ֗ז\rb* \rb you will discern|תָּ֭בִין\rb* \rb righteousness|צֶ֣דֶק\rb*
\q2 \rb and justice|וּמִשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb* \rb and equity|וּ֝מֵישָׁרִ֗ים\rb*— \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb good|טֽוֹב׃\rb* \rb path|מַעְגַּל־\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֣ה\rb* \rb will enter|תָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb your heart|בְלִבֶּ֑ךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and knowledge|וְ֝דַ֗עַת\rb* \rb will delight|יִנְעָֽם׃\rb* \rb your soul|לְֽנַפְשְׁךָ֥\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb Discretion|מְ֭זִמָּה\rb* \rb will watch over you|תִּשְׁמֹ֥ר\rb*,\rb |עָלֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and understanding|תְּבוּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb will guard you|תִנְצְרֶֽכָּה׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 12 \rb to deliver you|לְ֭הַצִּ֣ילְךָ\rb* \rb from the way|מִדֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of evil|רָ֑ע\rb*,
\q2 \rb from the man|מֵ֝אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb who speaks|מְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb perversity|תַּהְפֻּכֽוֹת׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 13 \rb from those who leave|הַ֭עֹ֣זְבִים\rb* \rb the straight|יֹ֑שֶׁר\rb* \rb paths|אָרְח֣וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb to walk|לָ֝לֶ֗כֶת\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדַרְכֵי־\rb* \rb of darkness|חֹֽשֶׁךְ׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 14 \rb from those who enjoy|הַ֭שְּׂמֵחִים\rb* \rb doing|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb evil|רָ֑ע\rb*
\q2 \rb and rejoice|יָ֝גִ֗ילוּ\rb* \rb in the twistedness|בְּֽתַהְפֻּכ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of evil|רָֽע׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 15 \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb paths|אָרְחֹתֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb are crooked|עִקְּשִׁ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and whose ways|בְּמַעְגְּלוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb are devious|וּ֝נְלוֹזִ֗ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb It will rescue you|לְ֭הַצִּ֣ילְךָ\rb* \rb from the forbidden|זָרָ֑ה\rb* \rb woman|מֵאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*,\f + \fr 2:16 \ft Or \fqa wayward wife\f*
\q2 \rb from the stranger|מִ֝נָּכְרִיָּ֗ה\rb*\f + \fr 2:16 \ft Or \fqa adulteress\f* \rb with seductive|הֶחֱלִֽיקָה׃\rb* \rb words|אֲמָרֶ֥יהָ\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb who abandons|הַ֭עֹזֶבֶת\rb* \rb the partner|אַלּ֣וּף\rb* \rb of her youth|נְעוּרֶ֑יהָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb and forgets|שָׁכֵֽחָה׃\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֖ית\rb* \rb of her God|אֱלֹהֶ֣יהָ\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb her house|בֵּיתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb sinks down|שָׁ֣חָה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb death|מָ֣וֶת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and her tracks|מַעְגְּלֹתֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the departed spirits|רְ֝פָאִ֗ים\rb*.\f + \fr 2:18 \ft Hebrew \fqa to the Rephaim\f*
\q1 \v 19 \rb None|כָּל־\rb* \rb who go to her|בָּ֭אֶיהָ\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb return|יְשׁוּב֑וּן\rb*
\q2 \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb negotiate|יַ֝שִּׂ֗יגוּ\rb* \rb the paths|אָרְח֥וֹת\rb* \rb of life|חַיִּֽים׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb So|לְמַ֗עַן\rb* \rb you will follow|תֵּ֭לֵךְ\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the good|טוֹבִ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and keep to|תִּשְׁמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb the paths|וְאָרְח֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the righteous|צַדִּיקִ֣ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the upright|יְשָׁרִ֥ים\rb* \rb will inhabit|יִשְׁכְּנוּ\rb* \rb the land|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the blameless|וּ֝תְמִימִ֗ים\rb* \rb will remain|יִוָּ֥תְרוּ\rb* \rb in it|בָֽהּ׃\rb*;
\q1 \v 22 \rb but the wicked|וּ֭רְשָׁעִים\rb* \rb will be cut off|יִכָּרֵ֑תוּ\rb* \rb from|מִמֶּֽנָּה׃פ\rb* \rb the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the unfaithful|וּ֝בוֹגְדִ֗ים\rb* \rb will be uprooted|יִסְּח֥וּ\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 Trust in the LORD with All Your Heart
\q1 \v 1 \rb My son|בְּ֭נִי\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb forget|תִּשְׁכָּ֑ח\rb* \rb my teaching|תּוֹרָתִ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb but let your heart|לִבֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb keep|יִצֹּ֥ר\rb* \rb my commandments|וּ֝מִצְוֺתַ֗י\rb*;
\q1 \v 2 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they will add|יוֹסִ֥יפוּ\rb* \rb length|אֹ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb to your days|יָ֭מִים\rb*,
\q2 \rb years|וּשְׁנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and peace|וְ֝שָׁל֗וֹם\rb* \rb to your life|חַיִּ֑ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb Never|אַֽל־\rb* \rb let loving devotion|חֶ֥סֶד\rb*\f + \fr 3:3 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f* \rb or faithfulness|וֶאֱמֶ֗ת\rb* \rb leave you|יַעַ֫זְבֻ֥ךָ\rb*;
\q2 \rb bind|קָשְׁרֵ֥ם\rb* \rb them|עַל־\rb* \rb around your neck|גַּרְגְּרוֹתֶ֑יךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb write them|כָּ֝תְבֵ֗ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the tablet|ל֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of your heart|לִבֶּֽךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb Then you will find|וּמְצָא־\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb and high regard|וְשֵֽׂכֶל־\rb*\rb |ט֑וֹב\rb*
\q2 \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb and man|וְאָדָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb Trust|בְּטַ֣ח\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לִבֶּ֑ךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and lean|תִּשָּׁעֵֽן׃\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb* \rb on|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb your own understanding|בִּֽ֝ינָתְךָ֗\rb*;
\q1 \v 6 \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your ways|דְּרָכֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb acknowledge Him|דָעֵ֑הוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and He|וְ֝ה֗וּא\rb* \rb will make|יְיַשֵּׁ֥ר\rb* \rb your paths straight|אֹֽרְחֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb Be|תְּהִ֣י\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb* \rb wise|חָכָ֣ם\rb* \rb in your own eyes|בְּעֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb*;
\q2 \rb fear|יְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֝הוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and turn away|וְס֣וּר\rb* \rb from evil|מֵרָֽע׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb This will bring|תְּהִ֣י\rb* \rb healing|רִ֭פְאוּת\rb* \rb to your body|לְשָׁרֶּ֑ךָ\rb*\f + \fr 3:8 \ft Hebrew \fqa navel \ft \f*
\q2 \rb and refreshment|וְ֝שִׁקּ֗וּי\rb*\f + \fr 3:8 \ft Or \fqa medicine\f* \rb to your bones|לְעַצְמוֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb Honor|כַּבֵּ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb with your wealth|מֵהוֹנֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and with the firstfruits|וּ֝מֵרֵאשִׁ֗ית\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your crops|תְּבוּאָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*;
\q1 \v 10 \rb then your barns|אֲסָמֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb will be filled|וְיִמָּלְא֣וּ\rb* \rb with plenty|שָׂבָ֑ע\rb*,
\q2 \rb and your vats|יְקָבֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb will overflow|יִפְרֹֽצוּ׃פ\rb* \rb with new wine|וְ֝תִיר֗וֹשׁ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb My son|בְּנִ֣י\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb reject|תִּמְאָ֑ס\rb* \rb the discipline|מוּסַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb loathe|תָּ֝קֹ֗ץ\rb* \rb His rebuke|בְּתוֹכַחְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*;\f + \fr 3:11 \ft LXX \fqa and do not lose heart when He rebukes\ft ; cited in \ref Hebrews 12:5|HEB 12:5\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 12 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶ֥ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb disciplines|יוֹכִ֑יחַ\rb* \rb the one|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He loves|יֶאֱהַ֣ב\rb*,
\q2 \rb as does a father|וּ֝כְאָ֗ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the son|בֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb in whom he delights|יִרְצֶֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 3:12 \ft LXX \fqa and He flogs every son He receives\ft ; cited in \ref Hebrews 12:6|HEB 12:6\ref*\f*
\s1 The Blessings of Wisdom
\q1 \v 13 \rb Blessed|אַשְׁרֵ֣י\rb* \rb is the man|אָ֭דָם\rb* \rb who finds|מָצָ֣א\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb the man|וְ֝אָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb who acquires|יָפִ֥יק\rb* \rb understanding|תְּבוּנָֽה׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 14 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb she is more|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb profitable|סַ֭חְרָהּ\rb*\rb |מִסְּחַר־\rb* \rb than silver|כָּ֑סֶף\rb*,
\q2 \rb and her gain is better|תְּבוּאָתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb than fine gold|וּ֝מֵחָר֗וּץ\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb She|הִ֭יא\rb* \rb is more precious|יְקָ֣רָה\rb* \rb than rubies|מִפְּנִיִּים\rb*;
\q2 \rb nothing|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb you desire|חֲ֝פָצֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb compares|יִֽשְׁווּ־\rb* \rb with her|בָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb Long|אֹ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb life|יָ֭מִים\rb* \rb is in her right hand|בִּֽימִינָ֑הּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb in her left hand|בִּ֝שְׂמֹאולָ֗הּ\rb* \rb are riches|עֹ֣שֶׁר\rb* \rb and honor|וְכָבֽוֹד׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb All her ways|דְּרָכֶ֥יהָ\rb*\rb |דַרְכֵי־\rb* \rb are pleasant|נֹ֑עַם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and all|וְֽכָל־\rb* \rb her paths|נְתִ֖יבוֹתֶ֣יהָ\rb* \rb are peaceful|שָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb She|הִ֭יא\rb* \rb is a tree|עֵץ־\rb* \rb of life|חַיִּ֣ים\rb* \rb to those who embrace|לַמַּחֲזִיקִ֣ים\rb* \rb her|בָּ֑הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and those who lay hold of her|וְֽתֹמְכֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb are blessed|מְאֻשָּֽׁר׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb The LORD|יְֽהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb founded|יָֽסַד־\rb* \rb the earth|אָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb by wisdom|בְּחָכְמָ֥ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and established|כּוֹנֵ֥ן\rb* \rb the heavens|שָׁ֝מַ֗יִם\rb* \rb by understanding|בִּתְבוּנָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb By His knowledge|בְּ֭דַעְתּוֹ\rb* \rb the watery depths|תְּהוֹמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb were broken open|נִבְקָ֑עוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the clouds|וּ֝שְׁחָקִ֗ים\rb* \rb dripped|יִרְעֲפוּ־\rb* \rb with dew|טָֽל׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb My son|בְּ֭נִי\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb lose|יָלֻ֣זוּ\rb* \rb sight of this|מֵעֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb*:
\q2 \rb Preserve|נְצֹ֥ר\rb* \rb sound judgment|תֻּ֝שִׁיָּ֗ה\rb* \rb and discernment|וּמְזִמָּֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb They will be|וְיִֽהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb life|חַיִּ֣ים\rb* \rb to your soul|לְנַפְשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and adornment|וְ֝חֵ֗ן\rb* \rb to your neck|לְגַרְגְּרֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb Then|אָ֤ז\rb* \rb you will go|תֵּלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb on your way|דַּרְכֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb in safety|לָבֶ֣טַח\rb*,
\q2 \rb and your foot|וְ֝רַגְלְךָ֗\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb stumble|תִגּֽוֹף׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb When|אִם־\rb* \rb you lie down|תִּשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb*, \rb you will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִפְחָ֑ד\rb*;
\q2 \rb when you rest|וְ֝שָׁכַבְתָּ֗\rb*, \rb your sleep|שְׁנָתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb will be sweet|וְֽעָרְבָ֥ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 25 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb fear|תִּ֭ירָא\rb* \rb sudden|פִּתְאֹ֑ם\rb* \rb danger|מִפַּ֣חַד\rb*
\q2 \rb or the ruin|וּמִשֹּׁאַ֥ת\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb overtakes|תָבֹֽא׃\rb* \rb the wicked|רְ֝שָׁעִ֗ים\rb*,
\q1 \v 26 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb your confidence|בְכִסְלֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and will keep|וְשָׁמַ֖ר\rb* \rb your foot|רַגְלְךָ֣\rb* \rb from the snare|מִלָּֽכֶד׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 27 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb withhold|תִּמְנַע־\rb* \rb good|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb from the deserving|מִבְּעָלָ֑יו\rb*\f + \fr 3:27 \ft Or \fqa from its owners\f*
\q2 \rb when it is|בִּהְי֨וֹת\rb* \rb within your|יָדֶיךָ\rb* \rb power|לְאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to act|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 28 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb tell|תֹּ֘אמַ֤ר\rb* \rb your neighbor|לְרֵעֶיךָ\rb*,
\q2 “\rb Come|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb back|וָ֭שׁוּב\rb* \rb tomorrow|וּמָחָ֥ר\rb* \rb and I will provide|אֶתֵּ֗ן\rb*”—
\q2 \rb when you already have the means|וְיֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אִתָּֽךְ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 29 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb devise|רָעָ֑ה\rb* \rb evil|תַּחֲרֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb your neighbor|רֵעֲךָ֣\rb*,
\q2 \rb for he|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb trustfully|לָבֶ֣טַח\rb* \rb dwells|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb beside you|אִתָּֽךְ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 30 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb accuse|תָּרוֹב\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb a man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb without cause|חִנָּ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb when|אִם־\rb* \rb he has done|גְמָלְךָ֣\rb* \rb you no|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb harm|רָעָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 31 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb envy|תְּ֭קַנֵּא\rb* \rb a violent|חָמָ֑ס\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb man|בְּאִ֣ישׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb or choose|תִּ֝בְחַ֗ר\rb* \rb any|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb of his ways|דְּרָכָֽיו׃\rb*;
\q1 \v 32 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb detests|תוֹעֲבַ֣ת\rb* \rb the perverse|נָל֑וֹז\rb*\rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb*,
\q2 \rb but He is a friend|סוֹדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb to the upright|יְשָׁרִ֥ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 33 \rb The curse|מְאֵרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb is on the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the wicked|רָשָׁ֑ע\rb*,
\q2 \rb but He blesses|יְבָרֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb the home|וּנְוֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of the righteous|צַדִּיקִ֣ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 34 \rb |אִם־\rb* \rb He|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb mocks|לַלֵּצִ֥ים\rb* \rb the mockers|יָלִ֑יץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but gives|יִתֶּן־\rb* \rb grace|חֵֽן׃\rb* \rb to the humble|וְלַעֲנִיִּים\rb*.\f + \fr 3:34 \ft LXX \fqa The Lord opposes the proud, but gives grace to the humble\ft ; cited in \ref James 4:6|JAS 4:6\ref* and 1 Peter 5:5\f*
\q1 \v 35 \rb The wise|חֲכָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb will inherit|יִנְחָ֑לוּ\rb* \rb honor|כָּ֭בוֹד\rb*,
\q2 \rb but fools|וּ֝כְסִילִ֗ים\rb* \rb are held up|מֵרִ֥ים\rb* \rb to shame|קָלֽוֹן׃פ\rb*.
\c 4
\s1 A Father’s Instruction
\q1 \v 1 \rb Listen|שִׁמְע֣וּ\rb*, \rb my sons|בָ֭נִים\rb*, \rb to a father’s|אָ֑ב\rb* \rb instruction|מ֣וּסַר\rb*;
\q2 \rb pay attention|וְ֝הַקְשִׁ֗יבוּ\rb* \rb and gain|לָדַ֥עַת\rb* \rb understanding|בִּינָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I give|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb sound|ט֭וֹב\rb* \rb teaching|לֶ֣קַח\rb*;
