\q2 \rb when the fountains|עִינ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the deep|תְּהוֹם׃\rb* \rb gushed forth|בַּ֝עֲז֗וֹז\rb*,
\q1 \v 29 \rb when He set|בְּשׂ֘וּמ֤וֹ\rb* \rb a boundary|חֻקּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb for the sea|לַיָּ֨ם׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that the waters|וּ֭מַיִם\rb* \rb would not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb surpass|יַֽעַבְרוּ־\rb* \rb His command|פִ֑יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb when He marked out|בְּ֝חוּק֗וֹ\rb* \rb the foundations|מ֣וֹסְדֵי\rb* \rb of the earth|אָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 30 \rb Then I was|וָֽאֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a skilled craftsman|אָ֫מ֥וֹן\rb* \rb at His side|אֶצְל֗וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and|וָֽאֶהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb His delight|שַׁ֭עֲשֻׁעִים\rb*\f + \fr 8:30 \ft Or \fqa filled with His delight\f* \rb day|י֤וֹם׀\rb* \rb by day|י֑וֹם\rb*,
\q2 \rb rejoicing|מְשַׂחֶ֖קֶת\rb* \rb always|בְּכָל־\rb*\rb |עֵֽת׃\rb* \rb in His presence|לְפָנָ֣יו\rb*.
\q1 \v 31 \rb I was rejoicing|מְ֭שַׂחֶקֶת\rb* \rb in His whole world|בְּתֵבֵ֣ל\rb*\rb |אַרְצ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb delighting|וְ֝שַׁעֲשֻׁעַ֗י\rb* \rb together|אֶת־\rb* \rb in the sons|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of men|אָדָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 32 \rb Now therefore|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb my sons|בָ֭נִים\rb*, \rb listen|שִׁמְעוּ־\rb* \rb to me|לִ֑י\rb*,
\q2 \rb for blessed|וְ֝אַשְׁרֵ֗י\rb* \rb are those who keep|יִשְׁמֹֽרוּ׃\rb* \rb my ways|דְּרָכַ֥י\rb*.
\q1 \v 33 \rb Listen|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb to instruction|מוּסָ֥ר\rb* \rb and be wise|וַחֲכָ֗מוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb ignore it|תִּפְרָֽעוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 34 \rb Blessed|אַ֥שְֽׁרֵי\rb* \rb is the man|אָדָם֮\rb* \rb who listens|שֹׁמֵ֪עַֽ֫\rb* \rb to me|לִ֥י\rb*,
\q2 \rb watching|לִשְׁקֹ֣ד\rb* \rb daily|י֤וֹם׀\rb*\rb |י֑וֹם\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb my doors|דַּ֭לְתֹתַי\rb*,
\q2 \rb waiting|לִ֝שְׁמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb at the posts|מְזוּזֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of my doorway|פְּתָחָֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 35 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb whoever finds me|מֹ֭צְאִי\rb* \rb finds|מֹצְאֵי\rb* \rb life|חַיִּ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and obtains|וַיָּ֥פֶק\rb* \rb the favor|רָ֝צ֗וֹן\rb* \rb of the LORD|מֵיְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 36 \rb But he who fails to find me|וְֽ֭חֹטְאִי\rb* \rb harms|חֹמֵ֣ס\rb* \rb himself|נַפְשׁ֑וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who hate me|מְ֝שַׂנְאַ֗י\rb* \rb love|אָ֣הֲבוּ\rb* \rb death|מָֽוֶת׃פ\rb*.”
\c 9
\s1 The Way of Wisdom
\r (\ref Proverbs 1:1–7|PRO 1:1-7\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb Wisdom|חָ֭כְמוֹת\rb* \rb has built|בָּנְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb her house|בֵיתָ֑הּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb she has carved out|חָצְבָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 9:1 \ft Hebrew; LXX, Syriac, and Aramaic Targum \fqa has set up\f* \rb her seven|שִׁבְעָֽה׃\rb* \rb pillars|עַמּוּדֶ֣יהָ\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb She has prepared|טָבְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb her meat|טִ֭בְחָהּ\rb* \rb and mixed|מָסְכָ֣ה\rb* \rb her wine|יֵינָ֑הּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb she has also|אַ֝֗ף\rb* \rb set|עָֽרְכָ֥ה\rb* \rb her table|שֻׁלְחָנָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb She has sent out|שָֽׁלְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb her maidservants|נַעֲרֹתֶ֣יהָ\rb*;
\q2 \rb she calls out|תִקְרָ֑א\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb*\rb |גַּ֝פֵּ֗י\rb* \rb the heights|מְרֹ֣מֵי\rb* \rb of the city|קָֽרֶת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 “\rb Whoever|מִי־\rb* \rb is simple|פֶ֭תִי\rb*, \rb let him turn in|יָסֻ֣ר\rb* \rb here|הֵ֑נָּה\rb*!”
\q2 \rb she says|אָ֣מְרָה\rb* \rb to him|לּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb who lacks|חֲסַר־\rb* \rb judgment|לֵ֝֗ב\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 “\rb Come|לְ֭כוּ\rb*, \rb eat|לַחֲמ֣וּ\rb* \rb my bread|בְֽלַחֲמִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and drink|וּ֝שְׁת֗וּ\rb* \rb the wine|בְּיַ֣יִן\rb* \rb I have mixed|מָסָֽכְתִּי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb Leave your folly|פְתָאיִ֣ם\rb* \rb behind|עִזְב֣וּ\rb*, \rb and you will live|וִֽחְי֑וּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb walk|וְ֝אִשְׁר֗וּ\rb* \rb in the way|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of understanding|בִּינָֽה׃\rb*.”
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb He who corrects|יֹ֤סֵ֨ר׀\rb* \rb a mocker|לֵ֗ץ\rb* \rb brings|לֹקֵ֣חַֽ\rb* \rb shame|קָל֑וֹן\rb* \rb on himself|ל֣וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb he who rebukes|וּמוֹכִ֖יחַ\rb* \rb a wicked man|לְרָשָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb taints himself|מוּמֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb rebuke|תּ֣וֹכַח\rb* \rb a mocker|לֵ֭ץ\rb*, \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb he will hate you|יִשְׂנָאֶ֑ךָּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb rebuke|הוֹכַ֥ח\rb* \rb a wise man|לְ֝חָכָ֗ם\rb*, \rb and he will love you|וְיֶאֱהָבֶֽךָּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb Instruct|תֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb a wise man|לְ֭חָכָם\rb*, \rb and he will be wiser|וְיֶחְכַּם־\rb* \rb still|ע֑וֹד\rb*;
\q2 \rb teach|הוֹדַ֥ע\rb* \rb a righteous man|לְ֝צַדִּ֗יק\rb*, \rb and he will increase|וְי֣וֹסֶף\rb* \rb his learning|לֶֽקַח׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb The fear|יִרְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb is the beginning|תְּחִלַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of wisdom|חָ֭כְמָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and knowledge|וְדַ֖עַת\rb* \rb of the Holy One|קְדֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb is understanding|בִּינָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb through wisdom|בִ֭י\rb*\f + \fr 9:11 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Aramaic Targum; Hebrew \fqa through me\f* \rb your days|יָמֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb will be multiplied|יִרְבּ֣וּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and years|שְׁנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb will be added|וְיוֹסִ֥יפוּ\rb* \rb to your life|חַיִּֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you are wise|חָ֭כַמְתָּ\rb*, \rb you are wise|חָכַ֣מְתָּ\rb* \rb to your own advantage|לָּ֑ךְ\rb*;
\q2 \rb but if you scoff|וְ֝לַ֗צְתָּ\rb*, \rb you alone|לְֽבַדְּךָ֥\rb* \rb will bear the consequences|תִשָּֽׂא׃\rb*.
\s1 The Way of Folly
\q1 \v 13 \rb The woman|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb named Folly|כְּ֭סִילוּת\rb* \rb is loud|הֹֽמִיָּ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb she is naive|פְּ֝תַיּ֗וּת\rb* \rb and knows|יָ֥דְעָה\rb* \rb nothing|וּבַל־\rb*\rb |מָּֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb She sits|וְֽ֭יָשְׁבָה\rb* \rb at the door|לְפֶ֣תַח\rb* \rb of her house|בֵּיתָ֑הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a seat|כִּ֝סֵּ֗א\rb* \rb in the heights|מְרֹ֣מֵי\rb* \rb of the city|קָֽרֶת׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 15 \rb calling out|לִקְרֹ֥א\rb* \rb to those who pass by|לְעֹֽבְרֵי־\rb*,\rb |דָ֑רֶךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb who make|הַֽ֝מְיַשְּׁרִ֗ים\rb* \rb their paths straight|אֹֽרְחוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 “\rb Whoever|מִי־\rb* \rb is simple|פֶ֭תִי\rb*, \rb let him turn in|יָסֻ֣ר\rb* \rb here|הֵ֑נָּה\rb*!”
\q2 \rb she says|וְאָ֣מְרָה\rb* \rb to him|לּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb who lacks|וַחֲסַר־\rb* \rb judgment|לֵ֝֗ב\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 “\rb Stolen|גְּנוּבִ֥ים\rb* \rb water|מַֽיִם־\rb* \rb is sweet|יִמְתָּ֑קוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and bread|וְלֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb eaten in secret|סְתָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb is tasty|יִנְעָֽם׃\rb*!”
\q1 \v 18 \rb But they do not|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb know|יָ֭דַע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the dead|רְפָאִ֣ים\rb*\f + \fr 9:18 \ft Hebrew \fqa the Rephaim\f* \rb are there|שָׁ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb that her guests|קְרֻאֶֽיהָ׃פ\rb* \rb are in the depths|בְּעִמְקֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Sheol|שְׁא֣וֹל\rb*.
\c 10
\s1 Solomon’s Proverbs: The Wise Son
\p \v 1 \rb The proverbs|מִשְׁלֵ֗י\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹ֫מֹ֥ה פ\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb A wise|חָ֭כָם\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb brings joy|יְשַׂמַּח־\rb* \rb to his father|אָ֑ב\rb*,
\q2 \rb but a foolish|כְּ֝סִ֗יל\rb* \rb son|וּבֵ֥ן\rb* \rb grief|תּוּגַ֥ת\rb* \rb to his mother|אִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb Ill-gotten|רֶ֑שַׁע\rb* \rb treasures|אוֹצְר֣וֹת\rb* \rb profit|י֭וֹעִילוּ\rb* \rb nothing|לֹא־\rb*,
\q2 \rb but righteousness|וּ֝צְדָקָ֗ה\rb* \rb brings deliverance|תַּצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb from death|מִמָּֽוֶת׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb The LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb*\rb |נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb does not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb let the righteous|צַדִּ֑יק\rb* \rb go hungry|יַרְעִ֣יב\rb*,
\q2 \rb but He denies|יֶהְדֹּֽף׃\rb* \rb the craving|וְהַוַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Idle|רְמִיָּ֑ה\rb* \rb hands|כַף־\rb* \rb make|עֹשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb one poor|רָ֗אשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but diligent|חָרוּצִ֣ים\rb* \rb hands|וְיַ֖ד\rb* \rb bring wealth|תַּעֲשִֽׁיר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb He who gathers|אֹגֵ֣ר\rb* \rb in summer|בַּ֭קַּיִץ\rb* \rb is a wise|מַשְׂכִּ֑יל\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֣ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb but he who sleeps|נִרְדָּ֥ם\rb* \rb during harvest|בַּ֝קָּצִ֗יר\rb* \rb is a disgraceful|מֵבִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb son|בֵּ֣ן\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Blessings|בְּ֭רָכוֹת\rb* \rb are on the head|לְרֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the righteous|צַדִּ֑יק\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the mouth|וּפִ֥י\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְ֝שָׁעִ֗ים\rb* \rb conceals|יְכַסֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb violence|חָמָֽס׃\rb*.\f + \fr 10:6 \ft Or \fqa but violence covers the mouth of the wicked\ft ; also in verse 11\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb The memory|זֵ֣כֶר\rb* \rb of the righteous|צַ֭דִּיק\rb* \rb is a blessing|לִבְרָכָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the name|וְשֵׁ֖ם\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb will rot|יִרְקָֽב׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb A wise|חֲכַם־\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֭ב\rb* \rb will receive|יִקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb commandments|מִצְוֺ֑ת\rb*,
\q2 \rb but foolish|וֶאֱוִ֥יל\rb* \rb lips|שְׂ֝פָתַ֗יִם\rb* \rb will come to ruin|יִלָּבֵֽט׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb He who walks|הוֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in integrity|בַּ֭תֹּם\rb* \rb walks|יֵ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb securely|בֶּ֑טַח\rb*,
\q2 \rb but he who perverts|וּמְעַקֵּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb his ways|דְּ֝רָכָ֗יו\rb* \rb will be found out|יִוָּדֵֽעַ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb He who winks|קֹ֣רֵֽץ\rb* \rb the eye|עַ֭יִן\rb* \rb causes|יִתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb grief|עַצָּ֑בֶת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and foolish|וֶאֱוִ֥יל\rb* \rb lips|שְׂ֝פָתַ֗יִם\rb* \rb will come to ruin|יִלָּבֵֽט׃\rb*.\f + \fr 10:10 \ft Or \fqa babbling fools will fall\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb The mouth|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of the righteous|צַדִּ֑יק\rb* \rb is a fountain|מְק֣וֹר\rb* \rb of life|חַ֭יִּים\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the mouth|וּפִ֥י\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְ֝שָׁעִ֗ים\rb* \rb conceals|יְכַסֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb violence|חָמָֽס׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb Hatred|שִׂ֭נְאָה\rb* \rb stirs up|תְּעוֹרֵ֣ר\rb* \rb dissension|מְדָנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וְעַ֥ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb but love|אַהֲבָֽה׃\rb* \rb covers|תְּכַסֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb transgressions|פְּ֝שָׁעִ֗ים\rb*.\f + \fr 10:12 \ft See \ref 1 Peter 4:8|1PE 4:8\ref*\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Wisdom|חָכְמָ֑ה\rb* \rb is found|תִּמָּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb on the lips|בְּשִׂפְתֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the discerning|נָ֭בוֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb but a rod|וְ֝שֵׁ֗בֶט\rb* \rb is for the back|לְגֵ֣ו\rb* \rb of him who lacks|חֲסַר־\rb* \rb judgment|לֵֽב׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb The wise|חֲכָמִ֥ים\rb* \rb store up|יִצְפְּנוּ־\rb* \rb knowledge|דָ֑עַת\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the mouth|וּפִֽי־\rb* \rb of the fool|אֱ֝וִיל\rb* \rb invites|קְרֹבָֽה׃\rb* \rb destruction|מְחִתָּ֥ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb The wealth|ה֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the rich man|עָ֭שִׁיר\rb* \rb is his fortified|עֻזּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb city|קִרְיַ֣ת\rb*,
\q2 \rb but poverty|רֵישָֽׁם׃\rb* \rb is the ruin|מְחִתַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of the poor|דַּלִּ֣ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb The labor|פְּעֻלַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the righteous|צַדִּ֣יק\rb* \rb leads to life|לְחַיִּ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the gain|תְּבוּאַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the wicked|רָשָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb brings punishment|לְחַטָּֽאת׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb Whoever heeds|שׁוֹמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb instruction|מוּסָ֑ר\rb* \rb is on the path|אֹ֣רַח\rb* \rb to life|לְ֭חַיִּים\rb*,
\q2 \rb but he who ignores|וְעוֹזֵ֖ב\rb* \rb reproof|תּוֹכַ֣חַת\rb* \rb goes astray|מַתְעֶֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb The one who conceals|מְכַסֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb hatred|שִׂ֭נְאָה\rb* \rb has lying|שָׁ֑קֶר\rb* \rb lips|שִׂפְתֵי־\rb*,
\q2 \rb and whoever spreads|וּמוֹצִ֥א\rb* \rb slander|דִ֝בָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is a fool|כְסִֽיל׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb When words|דְּ֭בָרִים\rb* \rb are many|בְּרֹ֣ב\rb*, \rb sin|פָּ֑שַׁע\rb* \rb is unavoidable|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יֶחְדַּל־\rb*,
\q2 \rb but he who restrains|וְחֹשֵׂ֖ךְ\rb* \rb his lips|שְׂפָתָ֣יו\rb* \rb is wise|מַשְׂכִּֽיל׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb The tongue|לְשׁ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the righteous|צַדִּ֑יק\rb* \rb is choice|נִ֭בְחָר\rb* \rb silver|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the heart|לֵ֖ב\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb has little worth|כִּמְעָֽט׃\rb*.
\b 
