\c 11
\s1 Dishonest Scales
\r (\ref Deuteronomy 25:13–16|DEU 25:13-16\ref*; \ref Ezekiel 45:10–12|EZK 45:10-12\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb Dishonest|מִ֭רְמָה\rb* \rb scales|מֹאזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb are an abomination|תּוֹעֲבַ֣ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but an accurate|שְׁלֵמָ֣ה\rb* \rb weight|וְאֶ֖בֶן\rb* \rb is His delight|רְצוֹנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb When pride|זָ֭דוֹן\rb* \rb comes|בָּֽא־\rb*, \rb disgrace|קָל֑וֹן\rb* \rb follows|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb*,
\q2 \rb but with|וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb humility|צְנוּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb comes wisdom|חָכְמָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb The integrity|תֻּמַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the upright|יְשָׁרִ֣ים\rb* \rb guides them|תַּנְחֵ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the perversity|וְסֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb of the faithless|בּוֹגְדִ֣ים\rb* \rb destroys them|וְשַׁדָּם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Riches|ה֭וֹן\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb are worthless|יוֹעִ֣יל\rb* \rb in the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of wrath|עֶבְרָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but righteousness|וּ֝צְדָקָ֗ה\rb* \rb brings deliverance|תַּצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb from death|מִמָּֽוֶת׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb The righteousness|צִדְקַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the blameless|תָּ֭מִים\rb* \rb directs|תְּיַשֵּׁ֣ר\rb* \rb their path|דַּרְכּ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the wicked|רָשָֽׁע׃\rb* \rb fall|יִפֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb by their own wickedness|וּ֝בְרִשְׁעָת֗וֹ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb The righteousness|צִדְקַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the upright|יְ֭שָׁרִים\rb* \rb delivers them|תַּצִּילֵ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the faithless|בֹּגְדִ֥ים\rb* \rb are trapped|יִלָּכֵֽדוּ׃\rb* \rb by their own desires|וּ֝בְהַוַּ֗ת\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb When the wicked|רָ֭שָׁע\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb dies|בְּמ֤וֹת\rb*, \rb his hope|תִּקְוָ֑ה\rb* \rb perishes|תֹּאבַ֣ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the hope|וְתוֹחֶ֖לֶת\rb* \rb of his strength|אוֹנִ֣ים\rb* \rb vanishes|אָבָֽדָה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb The righteous man|צַ֭דִּיק\rb* \rb is delivered|נֶחֱלָ֑ץ\rb* \rb from trouble|מִצָּרָ֣ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb* \rb the wicked man|רָשָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb goes in|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb With his mouth|בְּפֶ֗ה\rb* \rb the ungodly man|חָ֭נֵף\rb* \rb destroys|יַשְׁחִ֣ת\rb* \rb his neighbor|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but through knowledge|וּ֝בְדַ֗עַת\rb* \rb the righteous|צַדִּיקִ֥ים\rb* \rb are rescued|יֵחָלֵֽצוּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb When the righteous|צַ֭דִּיקִים\rb* \rb thrive|בְּט֣וּב\rb*, \rb the city|קִרְיָ֑ה\rb* \rb rejoices|תַּעֲלֹ֣ץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and when the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb perish|וּבַאֲבֹ֖ד\rb*, \rb there are shouts of joy|רִנָּֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb By the blessing|בְּבִרְכַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the upright|יְ֭שָׁרִים\rb* \rb a city|קָ֑רֶת\rb* \rb is built up|תָּר֣וּם\rb*,
\q2 \rb but by the mouth|וּבְפִ֥י\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְ֝שָׁעִ֗ים\rb* \rb it is torn down|תֵּהָרֵֽס׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb Whoever shows contempt|בָּז־\rb* \rb for his neighbor|לְרֵעֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb lacks|חֲסַר־\rb* \rb judgment|לֵ֑ב\rb*,
\q2 \rb but a man|וְאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb of understanding|תְּבוּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb remains silent|יַחֲרִֽישׁ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb A gossip|רָ֭כִיל\rb*\rb |הוֹלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb reveals|מְגַלֶּה־\rb* \rb a secret|סּ֑וֹד\rb*,
\q2 \rb but a trustworthy|וְנֶאֱמַן־\rb* \rb person|ר֝֗וּחַ\rb* \rb keeps|מְכַסֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb a confidence|דָבָֽר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb For lack|בְּאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of guidance|תַּ֭חְבֻּלוֹת\rb*, \rb a nation|עָ֑ם\rb* \rb falls|יִפָּל־\rb*,
\q2 \rb but with many|בְּרֹ֣ב\rb* \rb counselors|יוֹעֵֽץ׃\rb* \rb comes deliverance|וּ֝תְשׁוּעָ֗ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb He who puts up security|עָ֣רַב\rb* \rb for a stranger|זָ֑ר\rb* \rb will surely suffer|רַע־\rb*\rb |יֵ֭רוֹעַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the one who hates|וְשֹׂנֵ֖א\rb* \rb indebtedness|תֹקְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb is secure|בּוֹטֵֽחַ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb A gracious|חֵ֭ן\rb* \rb woman|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb attains|תִּתְמֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb honor|כָּב֑וֹד\rb*,
\q2 \rb but ruthless men|וְ֝עָרִיצִ֗ים\rb* \rb gain|יִתְמְכוּ־\rb* \rb only wealth|עֹֽשֶׁר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb A kind|חָ֑סֶד\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb benefits|גֹּמֵ֣ל\rb* \rb himself|נַ֭פְשׁוֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but a cruel man|אַכְזָרִֽי׃\rb* \rb brings trouble|וְעֹכֵ֥ר\rb* \rb on himself|שְׁ֝אֵר֗וֹ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb The wicked man|רָשָׁ֗ע\rb* \rb earns|עֹשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb an empty|שָׁ֑קֶר\rb* \rb wage|פְעֻלַּת־\rb*,
\q2 \rb but he who sows|וְזֹרֵ֥עַ\rb* \rb righteousness|צְ֝דָקָ֗ה\rb* \rb reaps a true|אֱמֶֽת׃\rb* \rb reward|שֶׂ֣כֶר\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb Genuine|כֵּן־\rb* \rb righteousness|צְדָקָ֥ה\rb* \rb leads to life|לְחַיִּ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the pursuit|וּמְרַדֵּ֖ף\rb* \rb of evil|רָעָ֣ה\rb* \rb brings death|לְמוֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb The perverse|עִקְּשֵׁי־\rb* \rb in heart|לֵ֑ב\rb* \rb are an abomination|תּוֹעֲבַ֣ת\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the blameless|תְּמִ֣ימֵי\rb* \rb in their walk|דָֽרֶךְ׃\rb* \rb are His delight|וּ֝רְצוֹנ֗וֹ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb Be assured|יָ֣ד\rb*\rb |לְ֭יָד\rb* \rb that the wicked|רָּ֑ע\rb* \rb will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb go unpunished|יִנָּ֣קֶה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the offspring|וְזֶ֖רַע\rb* \rb of the righteous|צַדִּיקִ֣ים\rb* \rb will escape|נִמְלָֽט׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb Like a gold|זָ֭הָב\rb* \rb ring|נֶ֣זֶם\rb* \rb in a pig’s|חֲזִ֑יר\rb* \rb snout|בְּאַ֣ף\rb*
\q2 \rb is a beautiful|יָ֝פָ֗ה\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb who lacks|וְסָ֣רַת\rb* \rb discretion|טָֽעַם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 23 \rb The desire|תַּאֲוַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the righteous|צַדִּיקִ֣ים\rb* \rb leads only|אַךְ־\rb* \rb to good|ט֑וֹב\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the hope|תִּקְוַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb brings wrath|עֶבְרָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 24 \rb |יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb One gives freely|מְ֭פַזֵּר\rb*, \rb yet gains|וְנוֹסָ֥ף\rb* \rb even more|ע֑וֹד\rb*;
\q2 \rb another withholds|וְחוֹשֵׂ֥ךְ\rb* \rb what is right|מִ֝יֹּ֗שֶׁר\rb*, \rb only|אַךְ־\rb* \rb to become poor|לְמַחְסֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 25 \rb A generous|בְּרָכָ֥ה\rb* \rb soul|נֶֽפֶשׁ־\rb* \rb will prosper|תְדֻשָּׁ֑ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and he who refreshes others|וּ֝מַרְוֶ֗ה\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb will himself|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb be refreshed|יוֹרֶֽא׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 26 \rb The people|לְא֑וֹם\rb* \rb will curse|יִקְּבֻ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the hoarder|מֹ֣נֵֽעַ\rb* \rb of grain|בָּ֭ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb but blessing|וּ֝בְרָכָ֗ה\rb* \rb will crown|לְרֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb the one who sells it|מַשְׁבִּֽיר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 27 \rb He who searches out|שֹׁ֣חֵֽר\rb* \rb good|ט֭וֹב\rb* \rb finds|יְבַקֵּ֣שׁ\rb* \rb favor|רָצ֑וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb but evil|רָעָ֣ה\rb* \rb will come|תְבוֹאֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb to him who seeks it|וְדֹרֵ֖שׁ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 28 \rb He who trusts|בּוֹטֵ֣חַ\rb* \rb in his riches|בְּ֭עָשְׁרוֹ\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb will fall|יִפֹּ֑ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the righteous|צַדִּיקִ֥ים\rb* \rb will thrive|יִפְרָֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb like foliage|וְ֝כֶעָלֶ֗ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 29 \rb He who brings trouble|עוֹכֵ֣ר\rb* \rb on his house|בֵּ֭יתוֹ\rb* \rb will inherit|יִנְחַל־\rb* \rb the wind|ר֑וּחַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the fool|אֱ֝וִ֗יל\rb* \rb will be servant|וְעֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb to the wise|לַחֲכַם־\rb* \rb of heart|לֵֽב׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 30 \rb The fruit|פְּֽרִי־\rb* \rb of the righteous|צַ֭דִּיק\rb* \rb is a tree|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb of life|חַיִּ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and he who wins|וְלֹקֵ֖חַ\rb* \rb souls|נְפָשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb is wise|חָכָֽם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 31 \rb If|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb the righteous|צַ֭דִּיק\rb* \rb receive their due|יְשֻׁלָּ֑ם\rb* \rb on earth|בָּאָ֣רֶץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb how much more|אַ֝֗ף\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the ungodly|רָשָׁ֥ע\rb* \rb and the sinner|וְחוֹטֵֽא׃\rb*!\f + \fr 11:31 \ft LXX \fqa If it is hard for the righteous to be saved, what will become of the ungodly and the sinner?\ft Cited in \ref 1 Peter 4:18|1PE 4:18\ref*\f*
\c 12
\s1 Loving Discipline and Knowledge
\q1 \v 1 \rb Whoever loves|אֹהֵ֣ב\rb* \rb discipline|מ֭וּסָר\rb* \rb loves|אֹ֣הֵֽב\rb* \rb knowledge|דָּ֑עַת\rb*,
\q2 \rb but he who hates|וְשֹׂנֵ֖א\rb* \rb correction|תוֹכַ֣חַת\rb* \rb is stupid|בָּֽעַר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb The good man|ט֗וֹב\rb* \rb obtains|יָפִ֣יק\rb* \rb favor|רָ֭צוֹן\rb* \rb from the LORD|מֵיְהוָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the LORD condemns|יַרְשִֽׁיעַ׃\rb* \rb a man|וְאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb who devises evil|מְזִמּ֣וֹת\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb A man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb cannot|לֹא־\rb* \rb be established|יִכּ֣וֹן\rb* \rb through wickedness|בְּרֶ֑שַׁע\rb*,
