\q1 \v 15 \rb Justice|מִשְׁפָּ֑ט\rb* \rb executed|עֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb is a joy|שִׂמְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb to the righteous|לַ֭צַּדִּיק\rb*,
\q2 \rb but a terror|וּ֝מְחִתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb to the workers|לְפֹ֣עֲלֵי\rb* \rb of iniquity|אָֽוֶן׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb The man|אָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb who strays|תּ֭וֹעֶה\rb* \rb from the path|מִדֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of understanding|הַשְׂכֵּ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb will rest|יָנֽוּחַ׃\rb* \rb in the assembly|בִּקְהַ֖ל\rb* \rb of the dead|רְפָאִ֣ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb He who loves|אֹהֵ֣ב\rb* \rb pleasure|שִׂמְחָ֑ה\rb* \rb will become poor|מַ֭חְסוֹר\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb*;
\q2 \rb the one who loves|אֹהֵ֥ב\rb* \rb wine|יַֽיִן־\rb* \rb and oil|וָ֝שֶׁ֗מֶן\rb* \rb will never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be rich|יַעֲשִֽׁיר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb The wicked|רָשָׁ֑ע\rb* \rb become a ransom|כֹּ֣פֶר\rb* \rb for the righteous|לַצַּדִּ֣יק\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the faithless|בּוֹגֵֽד׃\rb* \rb for|וְתַ֖חַת\rb* \rb the upright|יְשָׁרִ֣ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb Better|ט֗וֹב\rb* \rb to live|שֶׁ֥בֶת\rb* \rb in the desert|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb*\rb |מִדְבָּ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb than with a contentious|מְדוֹנִים\rb* \rb and ill-tempered|וָכָֽעַס׃\rb* \rb wife|מֵאֵ֖שֶׁת\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb Precious|נֶחְמָ֣ד\rb* \rb treasures|אוֹצָ֤ר׀\rb* \rb and oil|וָ֭שֶׁמֶן\rb* \rb are in the dwelling|בִּנְוֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the wise|חָכָ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb but a foolish|וּכְסִ֖יל\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb consumes them|יְבַלְּעֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb He who pursues|רֹ֭דֵף\rb* \rb righteousness|צְדָקָ֣ה\rb* \rb and loving devotion|וָחָ֑סֶד\rb*
\q2 \rb finds|יִמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb life|חַ֝יִּ֗ים\rb*, \rb righteousness|צְדָקָ֥ה\rb*, \rb and honor|וְכָבֽוֹד׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb A wise man|חָכָ֑ם\rb* \rb scales|עָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb the city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of the mighty|גִּ֭בֹּרִים\rb*
\q2 \rb and pulls down|וַ֝יֹּ֗רֶד\rb* \rb the stronghold|עֹ֣ז\rb* \rb in which they trust|מִבְטֶחָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 23 \rb He who guards|שֹׁמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb his mouth|פִּ֭יו\rb* \rb and tongue|וּלְשׁוֹנ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb keeps|שֹׁמֵ֖ר\rb* \rb his soul|נַפְשֽׁוֹ׃\rb* \rb from distress|מִצָּר֣וֹת\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 24 \rb Mocker|לֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb is the name|שְׁמ֑וֹ\rb* \rb of the proud|זֵ֣ד\rb* \rb and arrogant man|יָ֭הִיר\rb* —
\q2 \rb of him who acts|ע֝וֹשֶׂ֗ה\rb* \rb with excessive|בְּעֶבְרַ֥ת\rb* \rb pride|זָדֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 25 \rb The craving|תַּאֲוַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the slacker|עָצֵ֣ל\rb* \rb kills him|תְּמִיתֶ֑נּוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb his hands|יָדָ֣יו\rb* \rb refuse|מֵאֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb to work|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb day long|הַ֭יּוֹם\rb* \rb he covets|הִתְאַוָּ֣ה\rb* \rb more|תַאֲוָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the righteous|וְצַדִּ֥יק\rb* \rb give|יִ֝תֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb without|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb restraint|יַחְשֹֽׂךְ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 27 \rb The sacrifice|זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְ֭שָׁעִים\rb* \rb is detestable|תּוֹעֵבָ֑ה\rb*—
\q2 \rb how much more so|אַ֝֗ף\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb brought|יְבִיאֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb with ill intent|בְזִמָּ֥ה\rb*!
\b 
\q1 \v 28 \rb A lying|כְּזָבִ֥ים\rb* \rb witness|עֵד־\rb* \rb will perish|יֹאבֵ֑ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the man|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb who listens to truth|שׁוֹמֵעַ\rb* \rb will speak|יְדַבֵּֽר׃\rb* \rb forever|לָנֶ֥צַח\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 29 \rb A wicked|רָשָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb hardens|הֵעֵ֬ז\rb* \rb his face|בְּפָנָ֑יו\rb*,\f + \fr 21:29 \ft Or \fqa puts up a bold front\f*
\q2 \rb but the upright man|וְ֝יָשָׁ֗ר\rb*\rb |ה֤וּא׀\rb* \rb makes|יָכִין\rb* \rb his way sure|דְּרָכָיו׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 30 \rb There is no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb wisdom|חָ֭כְמָה\rb*, \rb no|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb understanding|תְּבוּנָ֑ה\rb*, \rb no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb counsel|עֵ֝צָ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb that can prevail against|לְנֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 31 \rb A horse|ס֗וּס\rb* \rb is prepared|מ֭וּכָן\rb* \rb for the day|לְי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of battle|מִלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but victory|הַתְּשׁוּעָֽה׃\rb* \rb is of the LORD|וְ֝לַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb*.
\c 22
\s1 A Good Name
\q1 \v 1 \rb A good name|שֵׁ֭ם\rb* \rb is more desirable|נִבְחָ֣ר\rb* \rb than great|רָ֑ב\rb* \rb riches|מֵעֹ֣שֶׁר\rb*;
\q2 \rb favor|חֵ֣ן\rb* \rb is better|טֽוֹב׃\rb* \rb than silver|מִכֶּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וּ֝מִזָּהָ֗ב\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb The rich|עָשִׁ֣יר\rb* \rb and the poor|וָרָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb have this in common|נִפְגָּ֑שׁוּ\rb*:
\q2 \rb The LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb is Maker|עֹשֵׂ֖ה\rb* \rb of them all|כֻלָּ֣ם\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb The prudent|עָר֤וּם׀\rb* \rb see|רָאָ֣ה\rb* \rb danger|רָעָ֣ה\rb* \rb and take cover|וְיִסָּתֵר\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the simple|וּ֝פְתָיִ֗ים\rb* \rb keep going|עָבְר֥וּ\rb* \rb and suffer the consequences|וְֽנֶעֱנָֽשׁוּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb The rewards|עֵ֣קֶב\rb* \rb of humility|עֲ֭נָוָה\rb* \rb and the fear|יִרְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb are wealth|עֹ֖שֶׁר\rb* \rb and honor|וְכָב֣וֹד\rb* \rb and life|וְחַיִּֽים׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb Thorns|צִנִּ֣ים\rb* \rb and snares|פַּ֭חִים\rb* \rb lie on the path|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the perverse|עִקֵּ֑שׁ\rb*;
\q2 \rb he who guards|שׁוֹמֵ֥ר\rb* \rb his soul|נַ֝פְשׁ֗וֹ\rb* \rb stays far|יִרְחַ֥ק\rb* \rb from them|מֵהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Train up|חֲנֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb a child|לַ֭נַּעַר\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the way|דַרְכּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb he should go|פִּ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb and|גַּ֥ם\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he is old|יַ֝זְקִ֗ין\rb* \rb he will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb depart|יָס֥וּר\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּֽנָּה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb The rich|עָ֭שִׁיר\rb* \rb rule|יִמְשׁ֑וֹל\rb* \rb over the poor|בְּרָשִׁ֣ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the borrower|לֹ֝וֶ֗ה\rb*\rb |לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb is slave|וְעֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb to the lender|מַלְוֶֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb He who sows|זוֹרֵ֣עַ\rb* \rb injustice|עַ֭וְלָה\rb* \rb will reap disaster|יִקְצוֹר\rb*\rb |אָ֑וֶן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the rod|וְשֵׁ֖בֶט\rb* \rb of his fury|עֶבְרָת֣וֹ\rb* \rb will be destroyed|יִכְלֶֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 22:8 \ft LXX includes \fqa God blesses a cheerful and generous man, but foolish works will come to an end\ft ; see also \ref 2 Corinthians 9:7|2CO 9:7\ref*.\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb A generous man|טֽוֹב־\rb*\rb |עַ֭יִן\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb*\f + \fr 22:9 \ft Literally \fqa He whose eye is good\f* \rb will be blessed|יְבֹרָ֑ךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he shares|נָתַ֖ן\rb* \rb his bread|מִלַּחְמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb with the poor|לַדָּֽל׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Drive out|גָּ֣רֵֽשׁ\rb* \rb the mocker|לֵ֭ץ\rb*, \rb and conflict|מָד֑וֹן\rb* \rb will depart|וְיֵצֵ֣א\rb*;
\q2 \rb even quarreling|דִּ֣ין\rb* \rb and insults|וְקָלֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb will cease|וְ֝יִשְׁבֹּ֗ת\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb He who loves|אֹהֵ֥ב\rb* \rb a pure heart|טְהוֹר\rb*\rb |לֵ֑ב\rb* \rb and gracious|חֵ֥ן\rb* \rb lips|שְׂ֝פָתָ֗יו\rb*
\q2 \rb will have the king|מֶֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb for a friend|רֵעֵ֥הוּ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb The LORD’s|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb eyes|עֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb keep watch over|נָ֣צְרוּ\rb* \rb knowledge|דָ֑עַת\rb*,
\q2 \rb but He frustrates|וַ֝יְסַלֵּ֗ף\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the faithless|בֹגֵֽד׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb The slacker|עָ֭צֵל\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*, “\rb There is a lion|אֲרִ֣י\rb* \rb outside|בַח֑וּץ\rb*!
\q2 \rb I will be slain|אֵֽרָצֵֽחַ׃\rb* \rb in|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the streets|רְ֝חֹב֗וֹת\rb*!”
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb The mouth|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb of an adulteress|זָר֑וֹת\rb* \rb is a deep|עֲ֭מֻקָּה\rb* \rb pit|שׁוּחָ֣ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb he who is under the wrath|זְע֥וּם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְ֝הוָ֗ה\rb* \rb will fall|יִפּוֹל\rb* \rb into it|שָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb Foolishness|אִ֭וֶּלֶת\rb* \rb is bound up|קְשׁוּרָ֣ה\rb* \rb in the heart|בְלֶב־\rb* \rb of a child|נָ֑עַר\rb*,
\q2 \rb but the rod|שֵׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb of discipline|מ֝וּסָ֗ר\rb* \rb drives it far|יַרְחִיקֶ֥נָּה\rb* \rb from him|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb Oppressing|עֹ֣שֵֽׁק\rb* \rb the poor|דָּ֭ל\rb* \rb to enrich|לְהַרְבּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb oneself|ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb or giving gifts|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb to the rich|לְ֝עָשִׁ֗יר\rb*
\q2 \rb will surely lead|אַךְ־\rb* \rb to poverty|לְמַחְסֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\s1 Thirty Sayings of the Wise
\s2 Saying 1
\q1 \v 17 \rb Incline|הַ֥ט\rb* \rb your ear|אָזְנְךָ֗\rb* \rb and hear|וּ֭שְׁמַע\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the wise|חֲכָמִ֑ים\rb* —
\q2 \rb apply|תָּשִׁ֥ית\rb* \rb your mind|וְ֝לִבְּךָ֗\rb* \rb to my knowledge|לְדַעְתִּֽי׃\rb* —
\q1 \v 18 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it is pleasing|נָ֭עִים\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you keep them|תִשְׁמְרֵ֣ם\rb* \rb within you|בְּבִטְנֶ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |יִכֹּ֥נוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and they are constantly|יַ֝חְדָּ֗ו\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your lips|שְׂפָתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb So that your trust|מִבְטַחֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb may be|לִהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb in the LORD|בַּ֭יהוָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb I instruct you|הוֹדַעְתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* — \rb yes|אַף־\rb*, \rb you|אָֽתָּה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb Have I not|הֲלֹ֤א\rb* \rb written|כָתַ֣בְתִּי\rb* \rb for you|לְ֭ךָ\rb* \rb thirty sayings|שִׁלְשׁוֹם\rb*\f + \fr 22:20 \ft Or \fqa written for you excellent sayings \ft or \fqa written for you three times\f*
\q2 \rb about counsel|בְּמ֖וֹעֵצֹ֣ת\rb* \rb and knowledge|וָדָֽעַת׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 21 \rb to show you|לְהוֹדִֽיעֲךָ֗\rb* \rb true|קֹ֭שְׁטְ\rb* \rb and reliable|אֱמֶ֑ת\rb* \rb words|אִמְרֵ֣י\rb*,
\q2 \rb that you may|לְהָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb soundly|אֱ֝מֶ֗ת\rb* \rb answer|אֲמָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb those who sent you|לְשֹׁלְחֶֽיךָ׃פ\rb*?
\s2 Saying 2
\q1 \v 22 \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb rob|תִּגְזָל־\rb* \rb a poor|דָּ֭ל\rb* \rb man because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb is poor|דַל־\rb*,
\q2 \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb crush|תְּדַכֵּ֖א\rb* \rb the afflicted|עָנִ֣י\rb* \rb at the gate|בַשָּֽׁעַר׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 23 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb will take up|יָרִ֣יב\rb* \rb their case|רִיבָ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and will plunder|וְקָבַ֖ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb those who rob them|קֹבְעֵיהֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |נָֽפֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\s2 Saying 3
\q1 \v 24 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb make friends|תִּ֭תְרַע\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb an angry|אָ֑ף\rb* \rb man|בַּ֣עַל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb associate|תָבֽוֹא׃\rb* \rb with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb a hot-tempered|חֵ֝מוֹת\rb* \rb man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*,
\q1 \v 25 \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb you may learn|תֶּאֱלַ֥ף\rb* \rb his ways|אָרְחָתוֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and entangle|וְלָקַחְתָּ֖\rb* \rb yourself|לְנַפְשֶֽׁךָ׃\rb* \rb in a snare|מוֹקֵ֣שׁ\rb*.
\s2 Saying 4
\q1 \v 26 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be|תְּהִ֥י\rb* \rb one who gives pledges|בְתֹֽקְעֵי־\rb*\rb |כָ֑ף\rb*,
\q2 \rb who puts up security|בַּ֝עֹרְבִ֗ים\rb* \rb for debts|מַשָּׁאֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you have nothing|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb with which|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb to pay|לְשַׁלֵּ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb should your bed|מִ֝שְׁכָּבְךָ֗\rb* \rb be taken|יִקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb from under you|מִתַּחְתֶּֽיךָ׃\rb*?
\s2 Saying 5
\q1 \v 28 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb move|תַּ֭סֵּג\rb* \rb an ancient|עוֹלָ֑ם\rb* \rb boundary stone|גְּב֣וּל\rb*
\q2 \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבוֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \rb have placed|עָשׂ֣וּ\rb*.
\s2 Saying 6
