\q2 \rb and a mocker|לֵֽץ׃\rb* \rb is detestable|וְתוֹעֲבַ֖ת\rb* \rb to men|לְאָדָ֣ם\rb*.
\s2 Saying 25
\q1 \v 10 \rb If you faint|הִ֭תְרַפִּיתָ\rb* \rb in the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of distress|צָרָ֗ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb how small|צַ֣ר\rb* \rb is your strength|כֹּחֶֽכָה׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 11 \rb Rescue|הַ֭צֵּל\rb* \rb those being led away|לְקֻחִ֣ים\rb* \rb to death|לַמָּ֑וֶת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and restrain|תַּחְשֽׂוֹךְ׃\rb* \rb those stumbling|וּמָטִ֥ים\rb* \rb toward the slaughter|לַ֝הֶ֗רֶג\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you say|תֹאמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb Behold|הֵן֮\rb*, \rb we did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֪עְנ֫וּ\rb* \rb about this|זֶ֥ה\rb*,”
\q2 \rb does not|הֲ‍ֽלֹא־\rb* \rb He|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb who weighs|תֹ֘כֵ֤ן\rb* \rb hearts|לִבּ֨וֹת׀\rb* \rb consider it|יָבִ֗ין\rb*?
\q1 \rb Does not the One|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb who guards|וְנֹצֵ֣ר\rb* \rb your life|נַ֭פְשְׁךָ\rb* \rb know|יֵדָ֑ע\rb*?
\q2 \rb Will He not repay|וְהֵשִׁ֖יב\rb* \rb a man|לְאָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb according to his deeds|כְּפָעֳלֽוֹ׃\rb*?
\s2 Saying 26
\q1 \v 13 \rb Eat|אֱכָל־\rb* \rb honey|דְבַ֣שׁ\rb*, \rb my son|בְּנִ֣י\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb it is good|ט֑וֹב\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the honeycomb|וְנֹ֥פֶת\rb* \rb is sweet|מָ֝ת֗וֹק\rb* \rb to your|עַל־\rb* \rb taste|חִכֶּֽךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb Know|דְּעֶ֥ה\rb* \rb therefore|כֵּ֤ן׀\rb* \rb that wisdom is sweet|חָכְמָ֗ה\rb* \rb to your soul|לְנַ֫פְשֶׁ֥ךָ\rb*.
\q2 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you find it|מָ֭צָאתָ\rb*, \rb there is|וְיֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb a future for you|אַחֲרִ֑ית\rb*,
\q2 \rb and your hope|וְ֝תִקְוָתְךָ֗\rb* \rb will never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be cut off|תִכָּרֵֽת׃פ\rb*.
\s2 Saying 27
\q1 \v 15 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb lie in wait|תֶּאֱרֹ֣ב\rb*, \rb O wicked man|רָ֭שָׁע\rb*, \rb near the dwelling|לִנְוֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the righteous|צַדִּ֑יק\rb*;
\q2 \rb do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb destroy|תְּשַׁדֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb his resting place|רִבְצוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb For though|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb a righteous man|צַדִּ֣יק\rb* \rb may fall|יִפּ֣וֹל\rb* \rb seven times|שֶׁ֨בַע׀\rb*, \rb he still gets up|וָקָ֑ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb but the wicked|וּ֝רְשָׁעִ֗ים\rb* \rb stumble|יִכָּשְׁל֥וּ\rb* \rb in bad times|בְרָעָֽה׃\rb*.
\s2 Saying 28
\q1 \v 17 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb gloat|תִּשְׂמָ֑ח\rb* \rb when your enemy|אוֹיְבֶיךָ\rb* \rb falls|בִּנְפֹ֣ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let your heart|לִבֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb rejoice|יָגֵ֥ל\rb* \rb when he stumbles|וּ֝בִכָּשְׁל֗וֹ\rb*,
\q1 \v 18 \rb or|פֶּן־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֭הוָה\rb* \rb will see|יִרְאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and disapprove|וְרַ֣ע\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינָ֑יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb and turn His wrath|אַפּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb away|וְהֵשִׁ֖יב\rb* \rb from him|מֵעָלָ֣יו\rb*.
\s2 Saying 29
\q1 \v 19 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb fret|תִּתְחַ֥ר\rb* \rb over evildoers|בַּמְּרֵעִ֑ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be envious|תְּ֝קַנֵּ֗א\rb* \rb of the wicked|בָּרְשָׁעִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb For|כִּ֤י׀\rb* \rb the evil man|לָרָ֑ע\rb* \rb has|תִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb future|אַחֲרִ֣ית\rb*;
\q2 \rb the lamp|נֵ֖ר\rb* \rb of the wicked|רְשָׁעִ֣ים\rb* \rb will be extinguished|יִדְעָֽךְ׃\rb*.
\s2 Saying 30
\q1 \v 21 \rb My son|בְּנִ֣י\rb*, \rb fear|יְרָֽא־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb and the king|וָמֶ֑לֶךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and do not|אַל־\rb* \rb associate|תִּתְעָרָֽב׃\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the rebellious|שׁוֹנִ֑ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they will bring|יָק֣וּם\rb* \rb sudden|פִ֭תְאֹם\rb* \rb destruction|אֵידָ֑ם\rb*.
\q2 \rb Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb knows|יוֹדֵֽעַ׃ס\rb* \rb what ruin|וּפִ֥יד\rb* \rb they can bring|שְׁ֝נֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*?
\s1 Further Sayings of the Wise
\p \v 23 \rb These|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb are sayings of the wise|לַֽחֲכָמִ֑ים\rb*:
\q1 \rb To show partiality|הַֽכֵּר־\rb*\rb |פָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb in judgment|בְּמִשְׁפָּ֣ט\rb*
\q2 \rb is not|בַּל־\rb* \rb good|טֽוֹב׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb Whoever tells|אֹ֤מֵ֨ר׀\rb* \rb the guilty|לְרָשָׁע֮\rb*, “\rb You|אָ֥תָּה\rb* \rb are innocent|צַדִּ֪יק\rb*”—
\q2 \rb peoples|עַמִּ֑ים\rb* \rb will curse him|יִקְּבֻ֥הוּ\rb*, \rb and nations|לְאֻמִּֽים׃\rb* \rb will denounce him|יִזְעָמ֥וּהוּ\rb*;
\q1 \v 25 \rb but it will go well|יִנְעָ֑ם\rb* \rb with those who convict the guilty|וְלַמּוֹכִיחִ֥ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and rich|טֽוֹב׃\rb* \rb blessing|בִרְכַּת־\rb* \rb will come|תָּב֥וֹא\rb* \rb upon them|וַֽ֝עֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 26 \rb An honest|נְכֹחִֽים׃\rb* \rb answer|דְּבָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb given|מֵ֝שִׁ֗יב\rb*
\q2 \rb is like a kiss|יִשָּׁ֑ק\rb* \rb on the lips|שְׂפָתַ֥יִם\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 27 \rb Complete|הָ֘כֵ֤ן\rb* \rb your outdoor|בַּח֨וּץ׀\rb* \rb work|מְלַאכְתֶּ֗ךָ\rb* \rb and prepare|וְעַתְּדָ֣הּ\rb* \rb your field|בַּשָּׂדֶ֣ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb after that|אַ֝חַ֗ר\rb*, \rb you may build|וּבָנִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb your house|בֵיתֶֽךָ׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 28 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb testify|תְּהִ֣י\rb*\rb |עֵד־\rb* \rb against your neighbor|בְּרֵעֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb without cause|חִנָּ֣ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and do not deceive|וַ֝הֲפִתִּ֗יתָ\rb* \rb with your lips|בִּשְׂפָתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 29 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb say|תֹּאמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb I will do|עָֽשָׂה־\rb* \rb to him|לִ֭י\rb*\rb |כֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he has done|אֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb to me|לּ֑וֹ\rb*;
\q2 \rb I will repay|אָשִׁ֖יב\rb* \rb the man|לָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb according to his work|כְּפָעֳלֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\b 
\q1 \v 30 \rb I went|עָבַ֑רְתִּי\rb* \rb past|עַל־\rb* \rb the field|שְׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of a slacker|אִישׁ־\rb*\rb |עָצֵ֣ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and by|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the vineyard|כֶּ֝֗רֶם\rb* \rb of a man|אָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb lacking|חֲסַר־\rb* \rb judgment|לֵֽב׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 31 \rb |וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb Thorns|קִמְּשֹׂנִ֗ים\rb* \rb had grown up|עָ֘לָ֤ה\rb* \rb everywhere|כֻלּ֨וֹ׀\rb*,
\q2 \rb thistles|חֲרֻלִּ֑ים\rb* \rb had covered|כָּסּ֣וּ\rb* \rb the ground|פָנָ֣יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the stone|אֲבָנָ֣יו\rb* \rb wall|וְגֶ֖דֶר\rb* \rb was broken down|נֶהֱרָֽסָה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 32 \rb I|אָ֭נֹכִֽי\rb* \rb observed|וָֽאֶחֱזֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and took it|אָשִׁ֣ית\rb* \rb to heart|לִבִּ֑י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I looked|רָ֝אִ֗יתִי\rb* \rb and received|לָקַ֥חְתִּי\rb* \rb instruction|מוּסָֽר׃\rb*:
\q1 \v 33 \rb A little|מְעַ֣ט\rb* \rb sleep|שֵׁ֭נוֹת\rb*, \rb a little|מְעַ֣ט\rb* \rb slumber|תְּנוּמ֑וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb a little|מְעַ֓ט׀\rb* \rb folding|חִבֻּ֖ק\rb* \rb of the hands|יָדַ֣יִם\rb* \rb to rest|לִשְׁכָּֽב׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 34 \rb and poverty|רֵישֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb will come upon you|וּבָֽא־\rb* \rb like a robber|מִתְהַלֵּ֥ךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and need|וּ֝מַחְסֹרֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb like a bandit|כְּאִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |מָגֵֽן׃פ\rb*.
\c 25
\s1 More Proverbs of Solomon
\p \v 1 \rb These are|אֵ֭לֶּה\rb* \rb additional|גַּם־\rb* \rb proverbs|מִשְׁלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb were copied by|הֶ֝עְתִּ֗יקוּ\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י׀\rb* \rb of Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֬ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb It is the glory|כְּבֹ֣ד\rb* \rb of God|אֱ֭לֹהִים\rb* \rb to conceal|הַסְתֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb a matter|דָּבָ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and the glory|וּכְבֹ֥ד\rb* \rb of kings|מְ֝לָכִ֗ים\rb* \rb to search it out|חֲקֹ֣ר\rb*\rb |דָּבָֽר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb As the heavens|שָׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb are high|לָ֭רוּם\rb* \rb and the earth|וָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb is deep|לָעֹ֑מֶק\rb*,
\q2 \rb so the hearts|וְלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb of kings|מְ֝לָכִ֗ים\rb* \rb cannot|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb be searched|חֵֽקֶר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Remove|הָג֣וֹ\rb* \rb the dross|סִיגִ֣ים\rb* \rb from the silver|מִכָּ֑סֶף\rb*,
\q2 \rb and a vessel|כֶּֽלִי׃\rb* \rb for a silversmith|לַצֹּרֵ֣ף\rb* \rb will come forth|וַיֵּצֵ֖א\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb Remove|הָג֣וֹ\rb* \rb the wicked|רָ֭שָׁע\rb* \rb from the king’s|מֶ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb presence|לִפְנֵי־\rb*,
\q2 \rb and his throne|כִּסְאֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb will be established|וְיִכּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb in righteousness|בַּצֶּ֣דֶק\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb exalt yourself|תִּתְהַדַּ֥ר\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵי־\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֑לֶךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb stand|תַּעֲמֹֽד׃\rb* \rb in the place|וּבִמְק֥וֹם\rb* \rb of great men|גְּ֝דֹלִ֗ים\rb*;
\q1 \v 7 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb it is better|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb to be told|אֲמָר־\rb*\rb |לְךָ֗\rb*, “\rb Come up|עֲ‍ֽלֵ֫ה\rb* \rb here|הֵ֥נָּה\rb*!”
\q2 \rb than to be demoted|מֵֽ֭הַשְׁפִּ֣ילְךָ\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the prince|נָדִ֑יב\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb Even what|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\f + \fr 25:7 \ft Or \fqa Even the one\f* \rb you have seen|רָא֣וּ\rb* \rb with your own eyes|עֵינֶֽיךָ׃\rb*,
\q2 \v 8 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb bring|תֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb hastily|מַ֫הֵ֥ר\rb* \rb to court|לָרִ֗ב\rb*.
\q1 \rb Otherwise|פֶּ֣ן\rb*, \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb will you do|תַּ֭עֲשֶׂה\rb* \rb in the end|בְּאַחֲרִיתָ֑הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb when your neighbor|רֵעֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb puts you to shame|בְּהַכְלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֹתְךָ֣\rb*?
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb Argue|רִֽ֭יבְךָ\rb* \rb your case|רִ֣יב\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb your neighbor|רֵעֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb without|אַל־\rb* \rb betraying|תְּגָֽל׃\rb* \rb another’s|אַחֵ֣ר\rb* \rb confidence|וְס֖וֹד\rb*,
\q1 \v 10 \rb lest|פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb he who hears you|שֹׁמֵ֑עַ\rb* \rb bring shame upon you|יְחַסֶּדְךָ֥\rb*,
\q2 \rb and your infamy|וְ֝דִבָּתְךָ֗\rb* \rb never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb go away|תָשֽׁוּב׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb A word|דָּ֝בָ֗ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb fitly|אָפְנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb spoken|דָּבֻ֥ר\rb*
\q2 \rb is like apples|תַּפּוּחֵ֣י\rb* \rb of gold|זָ֭הָב\rb* \rb in settings|בְּמַשְׂכִּיּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of silver|כָּ֑סֶף\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb Like an earring|נֶ֣זֶם\rb* \rb of gold|זָ֭הָב\rb* \rb or an ornament|וַחֲלִי־\rb* \rb of fine gold|כָ֑תֶם\rb*
\q2 \rb is a wise man’s|חָ֝כָ֗ם\rb* \rb rebuke|מוֹכִ֥יחַ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb a listening|שֹׁמָֽעַת׃\rb* \rb ear|אֹ֥זֶן\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Like the cold|כְּצִנַּת־\rb* \rb of snow|שֶׁ֨לֶג׀\rb* \rb in the time|בְּי֬וֹם\rb* \rb of harvest|קָצִ֗יר\rb*
\q2 \rb is a trustworthy|נֶ֭אֱמָן\rb* \rb messenger|צִ֣יר\rb* \rb to those who send him|לְשֹׁלְחָ֑יו\rb*;
\q2 \rb he refreshes|יָשִֽׁיב׃פ\rb* \rb the soul|וְנֶ֖פֶשׁ\rb* \rb of his masters|אֲדֹנָ֣יו\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb Like clouds|נְשִׂיאִ֣ים\rb* \rb and wind|וְ֭רוּחַ\rb* \rb without|אָ֑יִן\rb* \rb rain|וְגֶ֣שֶׁם\rb*
\q2 \rb is the man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb who boasts|מִ֝תְהַלֵּ֗ל\rb* \rb of gifts|בְּמַתַּת־\rb* \rb never given|שָֽׁקֶר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb Through patience|בְּאֹ֣רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אַ֭פַּיִם\rb* \rb a ruler|קָצִ֑ין\rb* \rb can be persuaded|יְפֻתֶּ֣ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and a gentle|רַ֝כָּ֗ה\rb* \rb tongue|וְלָשׁ֥וֹן\rb* \rb can break|תִּשְׁבָּר־\rb* \rb a bone|גָּֽרֶם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb If you find|מָ֭צָאתָ\rb* \rb honey|דְּבַ֣שׁ\rb*, \rb eat|אֱכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb just what you need|דַּיֶּ֑ךָּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb lest|פֶּן־\rb* \rb you have too much|תִּ֝שְׂבָּעֶ֗נּוּ\rb* \rb and vomit it up|וַהֲקֵֽאתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
