\q2 \rb is a man|אִ֝֗ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ין\rb* \rb does not|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb control|מַעְצָ֣ר\rb* \rb his temper|לְרוּחֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\c 26
\s1 Similitudes and Instructions
\q1 \v 1 \rb Like snow|כַּשֶּׁ֤לֶג׀\rb* \rb in summer|בַּקַּ֗יִץ\rb* \rb and rain|וְכַמָּטָ֥ר\rb* \rb at harvest|בַּקָּצִ֑יר\rb*,\rb |כֵּ֤ן\rb*
\q2 \rb honor|כָּבֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb befit|נָאוֶ֖ה\rb* \rb a fool|לִכְסִ֣יל\rb*.
\q1 \v 2 \rb Like a fluttering|לָ֭נוּד\rb* \rb sparrow|כַּצִּפּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb or darting|לָע֑וּף\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb swallow|כַּדְּר֣וֹר\rb*,
\q2 \rb an undeserved|חִ֝נָּ֗ם\rb* \rb curse|קִֽלְלַ֥ת\rb* \rb does not|לֹא\rb* \rb come to rest|תָבֹֽא׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb A whip|שׁ֣וֹט\rb* \rb for the horse|לַ֭סּוּס\rb*, \rb a bridle|מֶ֣תֶג\rb* \rb for the donkey|לַחֲמ֑וֹר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and a rod|וְ֝שֵׁ֗בֶט\rb* \rb for the backs|לְגֵ֣ו\rb* \rb of fools|כְּסִילִֽים׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 4 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb answer|תַּ֣עַן\rb* \rb a fool|כְּ֭סִיל\rb* \rb according to his folly|כְּאִוַּלְתּ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb or|פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb you yourself|אָֽתָּה׃\rb* \rb will be like him|תִּשְׁוֶה־\rb*\rb |לּ֥וֹ\rb*\rb |גַם־\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb Answer|עֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb a fool|כְ֭סִיל\rb* \rb according to his folly|כְּאִוַּלְתּ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb lest|פֶּן־\rb* \rb he become|יִהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb wise|חָכָ֣ם\rb* \rb in his own eyes|בְּעֵינָֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb Like cutting off|מְקַצֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb one’s own feet|רַ֭גְלַיִם\rb* \rb or drinking|שֹׁתֶ֑ה\rb* \rb violence|חָמָ֣ס\rb*
\q2 \rb is the sending|שֹׁלֵ֖חַ\rb* \rb of a message|דְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb by the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of a fool|כְּסִֽיל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb Like lame|מִפִּסֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb legs|שֹׁ֭קַיִם\rb* \rb hanging limp|דַּלְי֣וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb is a proverb|וּ֝מָשָׁ֗ל\rb* \rb in the mouth|בְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb of a fool|כְסִילִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb Like binding|כִּצְר֣וֹר\rb* \rb a stone|אֶ֭בֶן\rb* \rb into a sling|בְּמַרְגֵּמָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb is|כֵּן־\rb* \rb the giving|נוֹתֵ֖ן\rb* \rb of honor|כָּבֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb to a fool|לִכְסִ֣יל\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb Like a thorn|ח֭וֹחַ\rb* \rb that goes|עָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb into the hand|בְיַד־\rb* \rb of a drunkard|שִׁכּ֑וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb is a proverb|וּ֝מָשָׁ֗ל\rb* \rb in the mouth|בְּפִ֣י\rb* \rb of a fool|כְסִילִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Like an archer|רַ֥ב\rb* \rb who wounds|מְחֽוֹלֵֽל־\rb* \rb at random|כֹּ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb is he who hires|וְשֹׂכֵ֥ר\rb* \rb a fool|כְּ֝סִ֗יל\rb* \rb or|וְשֹׂכֵ֥ר\rb* \rb passerby|עֹבְרִֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb As a dog|כְּ֭כֶלֶב\rb* \rb returns|שָׁ֣ב\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb its vomit|קֵא֑וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 26:11 \ft Cited in \ref 2 Peter 2:22|2PE 2:22\ref*\f*
\q2 \rb so a fool|כְּ֝סִ֗יל\rb* \rb repeats|שׁוֹנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb his folly|בְאִוַּלְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb Do you see|רָאִ֗יתָ\rb* \rb a man|אִ֭ישׁ\rb* \rb who is wise|חָכָ֣ם\rb* \rb in his own eyes|בְּעֵינָ֑יו\rb*?
\q2 \rb There is more hope|תִּקְוָ֖ה\rb* \rb for a fool|לִכְסִ֣יל\rb* \rb than for him|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb The slacker|עָ֭צֵל\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*, “\rb A lion|שַׁ֣חַל\rb* \rb is in the road|בַּדָּ֑רֶךְ\rb*!
\q2 \rb A fierce lion|אֲ֝רִ֗י\rb* \rb roams|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the public square|הָרְחֹבֽוֹת׃\rb*!”
\q1 \v 14 \rb As a door|הַ֭דֶּלֶת\rb* \rb turns|תִּסּ֣וֹב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its hinges|צִירָ֑הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb so the slacker|וְ֝עָצֵ֗ל\rb* \rb turns on|עַל־\rb* \rb his bed|מִטָּתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb The slacker|עָצֵ֣ל\rb* \rb buries|טָ֘מַ֤ן\rb* \rb his hand|יָ֭דוֹ\rb* \rb in the dish|בַּצַּלָּ֑חַת\rb*;
\q2 \rb it wearies him|נִ֝לְאָ֗ה\rb* \rb to bring it back|לַֽהֲשִׁיבָ֥הּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his mouth|פִּֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb The slacker|עָצֵ֣ל\rb* \rb is wiser|חָכָ֣ם\rb* \rb in his own eyes|בְּעֵינָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb than seven men|מִ֝שִּׁבְעָ֗ה\rb* \rb who answer|מְשִׁ֣יבֵי\rb* \rb discreetly|טָֽעַם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb Like one who grabs|מַחֲזִ֥יק\rb* \rb a dog|כָ֑לֶב\rb* \rb by the ears|בְּאָזְנֵי־\rb*
\q2 \rb is a passerby|עֹבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb who meddles|מִ֝תְעַבֵּ֗ר\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb a quarrel|רִ֥יב\rb* \rb not|לֹּֽא־\rb* \rb his own|לֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb Like a madman|כְּֽ֭מִתְלַהְלֵהַּ\rb* \rb shooting|הַיֹּרֶ֥ה\rb* \rb firebrands|זִקִּ֗ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and deadly|וָמָֽוֶת׃\rb* \rb arrows|חִצִּ֥ים\rb*,
\q1 \v 19 \rb so|כֵּֽן־\rb* \rb is the man|אִ֭ישׁ\rb* \rb who deceives|רִמָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his neighbor|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and says|וְ֝אָמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb I|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb was only|הֲ‍ֽלֹא־\rb* \rb joking|מְשַׂחֵ֥ק\rb*!”
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb Without|בְּאֶ֣פֶס\rb* \rb wood|עֵ֭צִים\rb*, \rb a fire|אֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb goes out|תִּכְבֶּה־\rb*;
\q2 \rb without|וּבְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb gossip|נִ֝רְגָּ֗ן\rb*, \rb a conflict|מָדֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb ceases|יִשְׁתֹּ֥ק\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb Like charcoal|פֶּחָ֣ם\rb* \rb for embers|לְ֭גֶחָלִים\rb* \rb and wood|וְעֵצִ֣ים\rb* \rb for fire|לְאֵ֑שׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb so is a quarrelsome|מְדוֹנִים\rb* \rb man|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb for kindling|לְחַרְחַר־\rb* \rb strife|רִֽיב׃פ\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb The words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of a gossip|נִ֭רְגָּן\rb* \rb are like choice morsels|כְּמִֽתְלַהֲמִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb that|וְ֝הֵ֗ם\rb* \rb go down|יָרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb into the inmost being|חַדְרֵי־\rb*\rb |בָֽטֶן׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 23 \rb Like glaze|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb*\rb |סִ֭יגִים\rb* \rb covering|מְצֻפֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb an earthen vessel|חָ֑רֶשׂ\rb*
\q2 \rb are burning|דֹּלְקִ֣ים\rb*\f + \fr 26:23 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa smooth\f* \rb lips|שְׂפָתַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and a wicked|רָֽע׃\rb* \rb heart|וְלֶב־\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb A hateful man|שׂוֹנֵ֑א\rb* \rb disguises himself|יִנָּכֵ֣ר\rb* \rb with his speech|בִּשְׂפָתוֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but he lays up|יָשִׁ֥ית\rb* \rb deceit|מִרְמָֽה׃\rb* \rb in his heart|וּ֝בְקִרְבּ֗וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \v 25 \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he speaks|ק֭וֹלוֹ\rb* \rb graciously|יְחַנֵּ֣ן\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb believe|תַּֽאֲמֶן־\rb* \rb him|בּ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֖בַע\rb* \rb abominations|תּוֹעֵב֣וֹת\rb* \rb fill his heart|בְּלִבּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb Though his hatred|שִׂ֭נְאָה\rb* \rb is concealed|תִּכַּסֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb by deception|בְּמַשָּׁא֑וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb his wickedness|רָעָת֣וֹ\rb* \rb will be exposed|תִּגָּלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb in the assembly|בְקָהָֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb He who digs|כֹּֽרֶה־\rb* \rb a pit|שַּׁ֭חַת\rb* \rb will fall|יִפֹּ֑ל\rb* \rb into it|בָּ֣הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and he who rolls|וְגֹ֥לֵ֥ל\rb* \rb a stone|אֶ֝בֶן\rb* \rb will have it roll back|תָּשֽׁוּב׃\rb* \rb on him|אֵלָ֥יו\rb*.
\q1 \v 28 \rb A lying|שֶׁ֭קֶר\rb* \rb tongue|לְֽשׁוֹן־\rb* \rb hates|יִשְׂנָ֣א\rb* \rb those it crushes|דַכָּ֑יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb and a flattering|חָ֝לָ֗ק\rb* \rb mouth|וּפֶ֥ה\rb* \rb causes|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb ruin|מִדְחֶֽה׃\rb*.
\c 27
\s1 Do Not Boast about Tomorrow
\r (\ref James 4:13–17|JAS 4:13-17\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb boast|תִּ֭תְהַלֵּל\rb* \rb about tomorrow|בְּי֣וֹם\rb*\rb |מָחָ֑ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb you do not|לֹא־\rb* \rb know|תֵ֝דַ֗ע\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb a day|יֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb may bring|יֵּ֥לֶד\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb Let another|זָ֣ר\rb* \rb praise you|יְהַלֶּלְךָ֣\rb*, \rb and not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb your own mouth|פִ֑יךָ\rb*—
\q2 \rb a stranger|נָ֝כְרִ֗י\rb*, \rb and not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb your own lips|שְׂפָתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb A stone|אֶ֭בֶן\rb* \rb is heavy|כֹּֽבֶד־\rb* \rb and sand|הַח֑וֹל\rb* \rb is a burden|וְנֵ֣טֶל\rb*,
\q2 \rb but aggravation|וְכַ֥עַס\rb* \rb from a fool|אֱ֝וִ֗יל\rb* \rb outweighs them|כָּבֵ֥ד\rb* \rb both|מִשְּׁנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Wrath|חֵ֭מָה\rb* \rb is cruel|אַכְזְרִיּ֣וּת\rb* \rb and anger|אָ֑ף\rb* \rb is like a flood|וְשֶׁ֣טֶף\rb*,
