\q2 \rb and one whose way|דָּֽרֶךְ׃פ\rb* \rb is upright|יְשַׁר־\rb* \rb is detestable|וְתוֹעֲבַ֖ת\rb* \rb to the wicked|רָשָׁ֣ע\rb*.
\c 30
\s1 The Words of Agur
\p \v 1 \rb These are the words|דִּבְרֵ֤י׀\rb* \rb of Agur|אָג֥וּר\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Jakeh|יָקֶ֗ה\rb* — \rb the burden|הַמַּ֫שָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb that this man|הַ֭גֶּבֶר\rb* \rb declared|נְאֻ֣ם\rb* \rb to Ithiel|לְאִֽיתִיאֵ֑ל\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb I am weary, O God,|לְאִ֖יתִיאֵ֣ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and worn out|וְאֻכָֽל׃\rb*.\f + \fr 30:1 \ft Or \fqa declared to Ithiel: “I am weary, O God, but I can prevail. \ft (revocalizations); Hebrew \fqa declared to Ithiel—to Ithiel and Ucal:\f*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Surely|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I am|אָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb the most ignorant|בַ֣עַר\rb* \rb of men|מֵאִ֑ישׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I lack|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb the understanding|בִינַ֖ת\rb* \rb of a man|אָדָ֣ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb I have not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb learned|לָמַ֥דְתִּי\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I have no knowledge|וְדַ֖עַת\rb*\rb |אֵדָֽע׃\rb* \rb of the Holy One|קְדֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb Who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb has ascended|עָלָֽה־\rb* \rb to heaven|שָׁמַ֨יִם׀\rb* \rb and come down|וַיֵּרַ֡ד\rb*?
\q2 \rb Who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb has gathered|אָֽסַף־\rb* \rb the wind|ר֨וּחַ׀\rb* \rb in His hands|בְּחָפְנָ֡יו\rb*?
\q1 \rb Who|מִ֤י\rb* \rb has bound up|צָֽרַר־\rb* \rb the waters|מַ֨יִם׀\rb* \rb in His cloak|בַּשִּׂמְלָ֗ה\rb*?
\q2 \rb Who|מִ֭י\rb* \rb has established|הֵקִ֣ים\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the ends|אַפְסֵי־\rb* \rb of the earth|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*?
\q1 \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is His name|שְּׁמ֥וֹ\rb*, \rb and what|וּמַֽה־\rb* \rb is the name|שֶּׁם־\rb* \rb of His Son|בְּ֝נ֗וֹ\rb*—
\q2 \rb surely|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you know|תֵדָֽע׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 5 \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb word|אִמְרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of God|אֱל֣וֹהַּ\rb* \rb is flawless|צְרוּפָ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb He|ה֝֗וּא\rb* \rb is a shield|מָגֵ֥ן\rb* \rb to those who take refuge|לַֽחֹסִ֥ים\rb* \rb in Him|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb add|תּ֥וֹסְףְּ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb His words|דְּבָרָ֑יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb lest|פֶּן־\rb* \rb He rebuke|יוֹכִ֖יחַ\rb* \rb you|בְּךָ֣\rb* \rb and prove you a liar|וְנִכְזָֽבְתָּ׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb Two|שְׁ֭תַּיִם\rb* \rb things I ask|שָׁאַ֣לְתִּי\rb*\rb |מֵאִתָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb of You|מִ֝מֶּ֗נִּי\rb* —
\q2 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb refuse me|תִּמְנַ֥ע\rb* \rb before|בְּטֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb I die|אָמֽוּת׃\rb*:
\q1 \v 8 \rb Keep falsehood|שָׁ֤וְא׀\rb* \rb and deceitful|כָּזָ֡ב\rb* \rb words|וּֽדְבַר־\rb* \rb far|הַרְחֵ֬ק\rb* \rb from me|מִמֶּ֗נִּי\rb*.
\q2 \rb Give|תִּֽתֶּן־\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb* \rb neither|אַל־\rb* \rb poverty|רֵ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb nor riches|וָ֭עֹשֶׁר\rb*;
\q2 \rb feed me|הַ֝טְרִיפֵ֗נִי\rb* \rb with the bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb that is my portion|חֻקִּֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb Otherwise|פֶּ֥ן\rb*, \rb I may have too much|אֶשְׂבַּ֨ע׀\rb*
\q2 \rb and deny You|וְכִחַשְׁתִּי֮\rb*, \rb saying|וְאָמַ֗רְתִּי\rb*, ‘\rb Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb is the LORD|יְה֫וָ֥ה\rb*?’
\q1 \rb Or|וּפֶֽן־\rb* \rb I may become poor|אִוָּרֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and steal|וְגָנַ֑בְתִּי\rb*,
\q2 \rb profaning|וְ֝תָפַ֗שְׂתִּי\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of my God|אֱלֹהָֽי׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb slander|תַּלְשֵׁ֣ן\rb* \rb a servant|עֶ֭בֶד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his master|אֲדֹנוֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb or|פֶּֽן־\rb* \rb he will curse you|יְקַלֶּלְךָ֥\rb*, \rb and you will bear the guilt|וְאָשָֽׁמְתָּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb There is a generation|דּ֭וֹר\rb* \rb of those who curse|יְקַלֵּ֑ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb their fathers|אָבִ֣יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb bless|יְבָרֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb their mothers|אִ֝מּ֗וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb There is a generation|דּ֭וֹר\rb* \rb of those who are pure|טָה֣וֹר\rb* \rb in their own eyes|בְּעֵינָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb and yet unwashed|רֻחָֽץ׃\rb* \rb of their filth|וּ֝מִצֹּאָת֗וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb There is a generation|דּ֭וֹר\rb*— \rb how|מָה־\rb* \rb haughty|רָמ֣וּ\rb* \rb are their eyes|עֵינָ֑יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and pretentious|יִנָּשֵֽׂאוּ׃\rb* \rb are their glances|וְ֝עַפְעַפָּ֗יו\rb* —
\q1 \v 14 \rb there is a generation|דּ֤וֹר׀\rb* \rb whose teeth|שִׁנָּיו֮\rb* \rb are swords|חֲרָב֣וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb and whose jaws|מְֽתַלְּעֹ֫תָ֥יו\rb* \rb are knives|וּֽמַאֲכָל֪וֹת\rb*,
\q1 \rb devouring|לֶאֱכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb the oppressed|עֲנִיִּ֣ים\rb* \rb from the earth|מֵאֶ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the needy|וְ֝אֶבְיוֹנִ֗ים\rb* \rb from among men|מֵאָדָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb The leech|לַֽעֲלוּקָ֨ה׀\rb* \rb has two|שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb daughters|בָנוֹת֮\rb*:
\q2 \rb Give|הַ֤ב׀\rb* \rb and Give|הַ֥ב\rb*.
\p \rb There|הֵ֭נָּה\rb* \rb are three|שָׁל֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb things that are never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb satisfied|תִשְׂבַּ֑עְנָה\rb*, \rb four that|אַ֝רְבַּ֗ע\rb* \rb never|לֹא־\rb* \rb say|אָ֥מְרוּ\rb*, ‘\rb Enough|הֽוֹן׃\rb*!’:
\li1 \v 16 \rb Sheol|שְׁאוֹל֮\rb*,
\li1 \rb the barren|וְעֹ֪צֶ֫ר\rb* \rb womb|רָ֥חַם\rb*,
\li1 \rb land|אֶ֭רֶץ\rb* \rb never|לֹא־\rb* \rb satisfied|שָׂ֣בְעָה\rb* \rb with water|מַּ֑יִם\rb*,
\li1 \rb and fire|וְ֝אֵ֗שׁ\rb* \rb that never|לֹא־\rb* \rb says|אָ֥מְרָה\rb*, ‘\rb Enough|הֽוֹן׃\rb*!’
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb As for the eye|עַ֤יִן׀\rb* \rb that mocks|תִּֽלְעַ֣ג\rb* \rb a father|לְאָב֮\rb*
\q2 \rb and scorns|וְתָב֪וּז\rb* \rb obedience|לִֽיקֲּהַ֫ת־\rb* \rb to a mother|אֵ֥ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb may the ravens|עֹרְבֵי־\rb* \rb of the valley|נַ֑חַל\rb* \rb pluck it out|יִקְּר֥וּהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and young|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb vultures|נָֽשֶׁר׃פ\rb* \rb devour it|וְֽיֹאכְל֥וּהָ\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb There|הֵ֭מָּה\rb* \rb are three things|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb too wonderful|נִפְלְא֣וּ\rb* \rb for me|מִמֶּ֑נִּי\rb*, \rb four|וְאַרְבָּע\rb* \rb that I cannot|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb understand|יְדַעְתִּֽים׃\rb*:
\li1 \v 19 \rb the way|דֶּ֤רֶךְ\rb* \rb of an eagle|הַנֶּ֨שֶׁר׀\rb* \rb in the sky|בַּשָּׁמַיִם֮\rb*,
\li1 \rb the way|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb of a snake|נָחָ֗שׁ\rb* \rb on|עֲלֵ֫י\rb* \rb a rock|צ֥וּר\rb*,
\li1 \rb the way|דֶּֽרֶךְ־\rb* \rb of a ship|אֳנִיָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |בְלֶב־\rb* \rb at sea|יָ֑ם\rb*,
\li1 \rb and the way|וְדֶ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb of a man|גֶּ֣בֶר\rb* \rb with a maiden|בְּעַלְמָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb This|כֵּ֤ן׀\rb* \rb is the way|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb of an adulteress|אִשָּׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |מְנָ֫אָ֥פֶת\rb*:
\q2 \rb She eats|אָ֭כְלָה\rb* \rb and wipes|וּמָ֣חֲתָה\rb* \rb her mouth|פִ֑יהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and says|וְ֝אָמְרָ֗ה\rb*, ‘\rb I have done|פָעַ֥לְתִּי\rb* \rb nothing|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb wrong|אָֽוֶן׃פ\rb*.’
\p \v 21 \rb Under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb three things|שָׁ֭לוֹשׁ\rb* \rb the earth|אֶ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb trembles|רָ֣גְזָה\rb*, \rb under|וְתַ֥חַת\rb* \rb four|אַ֝רְבַּ֗ע\rb* \rb it cannot|לֹא־\rb*\rb |תוּכַ֥ל\rb* \rb bear up|שְׂאֵֽת׃\rb*:
\li1 \v 22 \rb |תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb a servant|עֶ֭בֶד\rb* \rb who|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb becomes king|יִמְל֑וֹךְ\rb*,
\li1 \rb a fool|וְ֝נָבָ֗ל\rb* \rb who|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb is filled|יִֽשְׂבַּֽע־\rb* \rb with food|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*,
\li1 \v 23 \rb |תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb an unloved woman|שְׂ֭נוּאָה\rb* \rb who|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb marries|תִבָּעֵ֑ל\rb*,
\li1 \rb and a maidservant|וְ֝שִׁפְחָ֗ה\rb* \rb who|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb supplants|תִירַ֥שׁ\rb* \rb her mistress|גְּבִרְתָּֽהּ׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Four|אַרְבָּ֣עָה\rb* \rb things on earth|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*\rb |וְ֝הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb are small|קְטַנֵּי־\rb*, \rb yet they|הֵ֭ם\rb* \rb are exceedingly|מְחֻכָּמִֽים׃\rb* \rb wise|חֲכָמִ֥ים\rb*:
\li1 \v 25 \rb The ants|הַ֭נְּמָלִים\rb* \rb are creatures|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of little|לֹא־\rb* \rb strength|עָ֑ז\rb*, \rb yet they store up|וַיָּכִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb their food|לַחְמָֽם׃\rb* \rb in the summer|בַקַּ֣יִץ\rb*;
\li1 \v 26 \rb the rock badgers|שְׁ֭פַנִּים\rb*\f + \fr 30:26 \ft Or \fqa the coneys \ft or \fqa the hyraxes\f* \rb are creatures|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of little|לֹא־\rb* \rb power|עָצ֑וּם\rb*, \rb yet they make|וַיָּשִׂ֖ימוּ\rb* \rb their homes|בֵּיתָֽם׃\rb* \rb in the rocks|בַסֶּ֣לַע\rb*;
\li1 \v 27 \rb the locusts|לָאַרְבֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb have no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb king|מֶ֭לֶךְ\rb*, \rb yet they all|כֻּלּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb advance|וַיֵּצֵ֖א\rb* \rb in formation|חֹצֵ֣ץ\rb*;
\li1 \v 28 \rb and the lizard|שְׂ֭מָמִית\rb* \rb can be caught|תְּתַפֵּ֑שׂ\rb* \rb in one’s hands|בְּיָדַ֣יִם\rb*, \rb yet it|וְ֝הִ֗יא\rb* \rb is found in the palaces|בְּהֵ֣יכְלֵי\rb* \rb of kings|מֶֽלֶךְ׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb There|הֵ֭מָּה\rb* \rb are three things|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb that are stately|מֵיטִ֣יבֵי\rb* \rb in their stride|צָ֑עַד\rb*, \rb and four that|וְ֝אַרְבָּעָ֗ה\rb* \rb are impressive|מֵיטִ֥בֵי\rb* \rb in their walk|לָֽכֶת׃\rb*:
\li1 \v 30 \rb a lion|לַ֭יִשׁ\rb*, \rb mighty|גִּבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb among beasts|בַּבְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb*, \rb refusing|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb to retreat|יָ֝שׁ֗וּב\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵי־\rb* \rb anything|כֹֽל׃\rb*;
\li1 \v 31 \rb a strutting rooster|זַרְזִ֣יר\rb*\rb |מָתְנַ֣יִם\rb*;
\li1 \rb |אוֹ־\rb* \rb a he-goat|תָ֑יִשׁ\rb*;
\li1 \rb and a king|וּ֝מֶ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb with his army|אַלְק֥וּם\rb* \rb around him|עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 30:31 \ft Or \fqa a king against whom there is no rising up\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 32 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you have foolishly|נָבַ֥לְתָּ\rb* \rb exalted yourself|בְהִתְנַשֵּׂ֑א\rb*
\q2 \rb or if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you have plotted evil|זַ֝מּ֗וֹתָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb put your hand|יָ֣ד\rb* \rb over your mouth|לְפֶֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 33 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb as the churning|מִ֪יץ\rb* \rb of milk|חָלָ֡ב\rb* \rb yields|י֘וֹצִ֤יא\rb* \rb butter|חֶמְאָ֗ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the twisting|וּֽמִיץ־\rb* \rb of the nose|אַ֭ף\rb* \rb draws|י֣וֹצִיא\rb* \rb blood|דָ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb so the stirring|וּמִ֥יץ\rb* \rb of anger|אַ֝פַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb brings forth|י֣וֹצִיא\rb* \rb strife|רִֽיב׃פ\rb*.”
\c 31
\s1 The Sayings for King Lemuel
\p \v 1 \rb These are the words|דִּ֭בְרֵי\rb* \rb of King|מֶ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb Lemuel|לְמוּאֵ֣ל\rb* — \rb the burden|מַ֝שָּׂ֗א\rb* \rb that|אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his mother|אִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb taught him|יִסְּרַ֥תּוּ\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb What shall I say|מַה־\rb*,\f + \fr 31:2 \ft Or \fqa What \ft or \fqa What are you doing\f* \rb O my son|בְּ֭רִי\rb*?
\q2 \rb What|וּמַֽה־\rb*, \rb O son|בַּר־\rb* \rb of my womb|בִּטְנִ֑י\rb*?
\q2 \rb What|וּ֝מֶה\rb*, \rb O son|בַּר־\rb* \rb of my vows|נְדָרָֽי׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 3 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb spend|תִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb your strength|חֵילֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb on women|לַנָּשִׁ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb or your vigor|וּ֝דְרָכֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb on those who ruin|לַֽמְח֥וֹת\rb* \rb kings|מְלָכִֽין׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb It is not|אַ֤ל\rb* \rb for kings|לַֽמְלָכִ֨ים׀\rb*, \rb O Lemuel|לְֽמוֹאֵ֗ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb it is not|אַ֣ל\rb* \rb for kings|לַֽמְלָכִ֣ים\rb* \rb to drink|שְׁתוֹ־\rb* \rb wine|יָ֑יִן\rb*,
\q2 \rb or for rulers|וּ֝לְרוֹזְנִ֗ים\rb* \rb to crave|אוֹ\rb* \rb strong drink|שֵׁכָֽר׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 5 \rb lest|פֶּן־\rb* \rb they drink|יִ֭שְׁתֶּה\rb* \rb and forget|וְיִשְׁכַּ֣ח\rb* \rb what is decreed|מְחֻקָּ֑ק\rb*,
\q2 \rb depriving|וִֽ֝ישַׁנֶּה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the oppressed|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |עֹֽנִי׃\rb* \rb of justice|דִּ֣ין\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Give|תְּנוּ־\rb* \rb strong drink|שֵׁכָ֣ר\rb* \rb to one who is perishing|לְאוֹבֵ֑ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb and wine|וְ֝יַיִן\rb* \rb to the bitter|לְמָ֣רֵי\rb* \rb in soul|נָֽפֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb Let him drink|יִ֭שְׁתֶּה\rb* \rb and forget|וְיִשְׁכַּ֣ח\rb* \rb his poverty|רִישׁ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and remember|יִזְכָּר־\rb* \rb his misery|וַ֝עֲמָל֗וֹ\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb more|עֽוֹד׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Open|פְּתַח־\rb* \rb your mouth|פִּ֥יךָ\rb* \rb for those with no voice|לְאִלֵּ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb the cause|דִּ֝֗ין\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the dispossessed|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |חֲלֽוֹף׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb Open|פְּתַח־\rb* \rb your mouth|פִּ֥יךָ\rb*, \rb judge|שְׁפָט־\rb* \rb righteously|צֶ֑דֶק\rb*,
\q2 \rb and defend the cause|וְ֝דִ֗ין\rb* \rb of the poor|עָנִ֥י\rb* \rb and needy|וְאֶבְיֽוֹן׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Virtues of a Noble Woman
\q1 \v 10 \rb A wife|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb*\f + \fr 31:10 \ft Verses 10–31 are an acrostic poem, each verse beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.\f* \rb of noble character|חַ֭יִל\rb*, \rb who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb can find|יִמְצָ֑א\rb*?
\q2 \rb She is far|וְרָחֹ֖ק\rb* \rb more precious|מִכְרָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb than rubies|מִפְּנִינִ֣ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb The heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb of her husband|בַּעְלָ֑הּ\rb* \rb trusts|בָּ֣טַח\rb* \rb in her|בָּ֭הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and he lacks|יֶחְסָֽר׃\rb* \rb nothing|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb of value|וְ֝שָׁלָ֗ל\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb She brings him|גְּמָלַ֣תְהוּ\rb* \rb good|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb harm|רָ֑ע\rb*
\q2 \rb all|כֹּ֝֗ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of her life|חַיֶּֽיה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb She selects|דָּ֭רְשָׁה\rb* \rb wool|צֶ֣מֶר\rb* \rb and flax|וּפִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and works|וַ֝תַּ֗עַשׂ\rb* \rb with eager|בְּחֵ֣פֶץ\rb* \rb hands|כַּפֶּֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb She is|הָ֭יְתָה\rb* \rb like the merchant|סוֹחֵ֑ר\rb* \rb ships|כָּאֳנִיּ֣וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb bringing|תָּבִ֥יא\rb* \rb her food|לַחְמָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb from afar|מִ֝מֶּרְחָ֗ק\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb She rises|וַתָּ֤קָם׀\rb* \rb while it is still|בְּע֬וֹד\rb* \rb night|לַ֗יְלָה\rb*
\q2 \rb to provide|וַתִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb food|טֶ֣רֶף\rb* \rb for her household|לְבֵיתָ֑הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and portions|וְ֝חֹ֗ק\rb* \rb for her maidservants|לְנַעֲרֹתֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb She appraises|זָמְמָ֣ה\rb* \rb a field|שָׂ֭דֶה\rb* \rb and buys it|וַתִּקָּחֵ֑הוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb from her earnings|מִפְּרִ֥י\rb*\rb |כַ֝פֶּ֗יהָ\rb* \rb she plants|נְטַע\rb* \rb a vineyard|כָּֽרֶם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb She girds herself|חָֽגְרָ֣ה\rb*\rb |מָתְנֶ֑יהָ\rb*\f + \fr 31:17 \ft Hebrew \fqa She girds her loins\f* \rb with strength|בְע֣וֹז\rb*
\q2 \rb and shows that her arms|זְרֹעוֹתֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb are strong|וַ֝תְּאַמֵּ֗ץ\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb She sees|טָ֭עֲמָה\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb her gain|סַחְרָ֑הּ\rb* \rb is good|ט֣וֹב\rb*,
\q2 \rb and her lamp|נֵרָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb extinguished|יִכְבֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb at night|בַלַּיִל\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb She stretches|שִׁלְּחָ֣ה\rb* \rb out her hands|יָ֭דֶיהָ\rb* \rb to the distaff|בַכִּישׁ֑וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb and grasps|תָּ֣מְכוּ\rb* \rb the spindle|פָֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb with her fingers|וְ֝כַפֶּ֗יהָ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb She opens|פָּרְשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb her arms|כַּ֭פָּהּ\rb* \rb to the poor|לֶעָנִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb and reaches out|שִׁלְּחָ֥ה\rb* \rb her hands|וְ֝יָדֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb to the needy|לָֽאֶבְיֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb When it snows|מִשָּׁ֑לֶג\rb*, \rb she has no|לֹא־\rb* \rb fear|תִירָ֣א\rb* \rb for her household|לְבֵיתָ֣הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they are all|כָל־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֝יתָ֗הּ\rb* \rb clothed|לָבֻ֥שׁ\rb* \rb in scarlet|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 31:21 \ft Or \fqa doubly clothed\f*
\q1 \v 22 \rb She makes|עָֽשְׂתָה־\rb* \rb coverings for her bed|מַרְבַדִּ֥ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb her clothing|לְבוּשָֽׁהּ׃\rb* \rb is fine linen|שֵׁ֖שׁ\rb* \rb and purple|וְאַרְגָּמָ֣ן\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb Her husband|בַּעְלָ֑הּ\rb* \rb is known|נוֹדָ֣ע\rb* \rb at the city gates|בַּשְּׁעָרִ֣ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb where he sits|בְּ֝שִׁבְתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb among|עִם־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵי־\rb* \rb of the land|אָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb She makes|עָ֭שְׂתָה\rb* \rb linen garments|סָדִ֣ין\rb* \rb and sells them|וַתִּמְכֹּ֑ר\rb*;
\q2 \rb she delivers|נָתְנָ֥ה\rb* \rb sashes|וַ֝חֲג֗וֹר\rb* \rb to the merchants|לַֽכְּנַעֲנִֽי׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 25 \rb Strength|עֹז־\rb* \rb and honor|וְהָדָ֥ר\rb* \rb are her clothing|לְבוּשָׁ֑הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and she can laugh|וַ֝תִּשְׂחַ֗ק\rb* \rb at the days|לְי֣וֹם\rb* \rb to come|אַחֲרֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb She opens|פָּתְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb her mouth|פִּ֭יהָ\rb* \rb with wisdom|בְחָכְמָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and faithful|חֶ֝֗סֶד\rb* \rb instruction|וְתֽוֹרַת־\rb* \rb is on|עַל־\rb* \rb her tongue|לְשׁוֹנָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb She watches over|צ֭וֹפִיָּה\rb* \rb the affairs|הֲלִיכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of her household|בֵּיתָ֑הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכֵֽל׃\rb* \rb the bread|וְלֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb of idleness|עַ֝צְל֗וּת\rb*.
\q1 \v 28 \rb Her children|בָ֭נֶיהָ\rb* \rb rise up|קָ֣מוּ\rb* \rb and call her blessed|וַֽיְאַשְּׁר֑וּהָ\rb*;
\q2 \rb her husband|בַּ֝עְלָ֗הּ\rb* \rb praises her as well|וַֽיְהַֽלְלָהּ׃\rb*:
\q1 \v 29 “\rb Many|רַבּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb daughters|בָּ֭נוֹת\rb* \rb have done|עָ֣שׂוּ\rb* \rb noble things|חָ֑יִל\rb*,
\q2 \rb but you|וְ֝אַ֗תְּ\rb* \rb surpass|עָלִ֥ית\rb* \rb them|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כֻּלָּֽנָה׃\rb*!”
\b 
\q1 \v 30 \rb Charm|הַ֭חֵן\rb* \rb is deceptive|שֶׁ֣קֶר\rb* \rb and beauty|הַיֹּ֑פִי\rb* \rb is fleeting|וְהֶ֣בֶל\rb*,
\q2 \rb but a woman|אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb who fears|יִרְאַת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֝הוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |הִ֣יא\rb* \rb is to be praised|תִתְהַלָּֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 31 \rb Give|תְּנוּ־\rb* \rb her|לָ֭הּ\rb* \rb the fruit|מִפְּרִ֣י\rb* \rb of her hands|יָדֶ֑יהָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and let her works|מַעֲשֶֽׂיהָ׃\rb* \rb praise her|וִֽיהַלְל֖וּהָ\rb* \rb at the gates|בַשְּׁעָרִ֣ים\rb*.
